    "passage": "POSITION AVAILABLE: ASSISTANT STORE MANAGER — NORDWICK BOOKS, EASTGATE BRANCH\n\nNordwick Books, an independent bookseller with five locations across the region, is seeking a full-time assistant store manager for its busiest branch at Eastgate Shopping Centre.\n\nReporting to the store manager, the successful candidate will supervise a team of eight sales associates, manage weekly inventory orders, coordinate author events and book club meetings, and handle customer inquiries that require special attention. The role includes one weekend shift per week and occasional evening hours during signing events.\n\nApplicants should have at least two years of supervisory experience in retail; experience in bookselling or publishing is an advantage but not essential. Strong organizational skills and genuine enthusiasm for books are a must. Familiarity with the BookTrack inventory system is desirable, though full training will be provided.\n\nWe offer a competitive salary, a 30 percent employee discount at all branches, three weeks of paid vacation, and a professional development allowance that may be used for industry conferences or courses. After one year of employment, staff become eligible for our profit-sharing program.\n\nTo apply, email a résumé and a brief cover letter describing a memorable bookselling or customer service experience to careers@nordwickbooks.com by July 31. Interviews will be conducted during the second week of August, and the selected candidate is expected to start on September 1. No phone inquiries, please.",
