    "passage": "NOTICE TO ALL RESIDENTS — MAPLECREST APARTMENTS\n\nScheduled Water Shutoff: Tuesday, July 15\n\nPlease be advised that the water supply to Buildings A and B will be shut off on Tuesday, July 15, from 9:00 A.M. to approximately 3:00 P.M. while contractors replace the aging main valve in the basement of Building A. Building C will not be affected.\n\nDuring the shutoff, no tap water will be available in the affected buildings, and residents are advised to store water for drinking and washing in advance. The fitness room showers in Building C will remain open all day, and bottled water will be available free of charge at the management office, limited to two bottles per apartment.\n\nWhen service resumes, residents may notice cloudy or discolored water for a short period. This is normal after valve work; simply run your cold-water taps for three to five minutes until the water runs clear. If discoloration continues beyond Wednesday morning, please report it to the maintenance line at extension 511.\n\nWe have scheduled this work for a weekday to minimize disruption, as our records show building occupancy is lowest at that time. The replacement is part of a larger plumbing upgrade that will continue through August; notices for future work will be posted at least one week in advance.\n\nThank you for your cooperation.\nMaplecrest Property Management",
