    "passage": "NOTICE — CHANGES TO STAFF PARKING AT DELMONT REGIONAL HOSPITAL\n\nEffective Monday, April 7, the staff parking arrangements at Delmont Regional Hospital will change as construction begins on the new outpatient wing. The current staff lot on the east side of the campus (Lot E) will close permanently to make way for the building's foundation.\n\nAll employees who currently hold Lot E permits will be reassigned to one of two locations. Clinical staff working overnight or rotating shifts will receive priority placement in the parking garage adjacent to the main entrance (Garage 1). All other staff will be assigned to the new satellite lot on Berkshire Road, located approximately 800 meters from the main campus. A complimentary shuttle will run between the satellite lot and the hospital's north entrance every ten minutes between 5:30 A.M. and midnight.\n\nReassignment letters with new permit stickers will be distributed through department offices during the week of March 24. Employees who do not receive a letter by March 28 should contact the security office at parking@delmontregional.org. Please note that vehicles displaying old Lot E permits in either new location after April 18 will receive a written warning, and repeat violations may result in towing at the owner's expense.\n\nEmployees who wish to reduce their commuting costs are reminded that the hospital subsidizes 50 percent of monthly public transit passes. Applications are available on the staff intranet under \"Benefits.\"",
