    "question": "What is one change described in the notice?",
    "passage": "NOTICE — RECYCLING PROGRAM UPDATE, CITY OF ELMSWORTH\n\nStarting February 1, the City of Elmsworth will simplify its curbside recycling program in response to resident feedback and rising processing costs. Please review the following changes, which apply to all single-family homes and buildings with fewer than eight units.\n\nFirst, residents will no longer need to separate paper from containers. All accepted recyclables — paper, cardboard, glass bottles, metal cans, and rigid plastics marked 1, 2, or 5 — may be placed together in the blue cart. The green cart previously used for paper will be collected by the city during the week of February 9 and reused in the yard-waste program.\n\nSecond, collection will move from every week to every other week, on the same weekday as your current pickup. A calendar showing your collection dates is enclosed with this notice and is also available at elmsworth.gov/recycling. Because carts will hold two weeks of material, households that regularly fill their cart may request a second blue cart at no charge by calling 555-0118 before March 15; after that date, additional carts will cost $40.\n\nFinally, plastic bags, foam packaging, and electronics remain unacceptable in the blue cart. These items can be dropped off at the Hartley Road transfer station on Saturdays from 8 A.M. to 2 P.M. Items placed in carts incorrectly are the leading cause of rejected loads, which cost the city $60,000 last year.\n\nQuestions? Contact the Public Works Department at recycle@elmsworth.gov.",
