    "passage": "City Launches Bike-Share Program\n\nMORELAND (April 14) — The Moreland Department of Transportation officially launched its long-awaited bike-share program on Saturday, placing 400 bicycles at 35 docking stations throughout the downtown and riverside districts. Residents and visitors can rent a bicycle using a mobile application or a credit card at any station kiosk. Rides under thirty minutes cost $2.50, while a monthly membership, priced at $18, allows unlimited short trips. Transportation director Howard Lim said the program is intended to reduce traffic congestion and provide a convenient option for short journeys. \"Nearly half of all car trips in Moreland are under three kilometers,\" Mr. Lim noted. \"Cycling is a practical alternative for many of these trips.\" The city plans to assess the program at the end of the year and, if ridership targets are met, expand it to the Eastgate and Hillcrest neighborhoods next spring. Local business owners have generally welcomed the initiative, although some have expressed concern about the loss of street parking spaces where several docking stations were installed.",
