    "passage": "Calloway Museum to Reopen After Renovation\n\nSILVERTON (March 3) — After fourteen months of renovation work, the Calloway Museum of Regional History will reopen to the public on April 9. The $6.2 million project, funded largely by a grant from the Hartwell Foundation, added a climate-controlled storage facility, an expanded children's discovery room, and a glass-walled café overlooking Riverside Park. Museum director Evelyn Cho said the renovation also addressed long-standing accessibility issues. \"Every gallery is now reachable by elevator, and we have added audio guides in five languages,\" she said. To mark the reopening, the museum will waive admission fees during the first weekend and host a series of talks by local historians. Attendance at the museum had declined steadily before the closure, falling from 95,000 annual visitors in 2019 to just 61,000 in 2023. Ms. Cho is optimistic that the new amenities will reverse that trend. \"Our goal is to welcome 100,000 visitors in our first full year back,\" she said. The museum will be open Tuesday through Sunday, and admission will remain free for children under twelve.",
