    "question": "Why did Ms. Adeyemi send the letter?",
    "passage": "Hollis & Dane Home Appliances\nCustomer Care Department\n1500 Industry Drive, Calverton\n\nMarch 21\n\nMr. Owen Nakamura\n78 Juniper Court\nCalverton\n\nDear Mr. Nakamura,\n\nThank you for your letter of March 14 regarding the dishwasher (model HD-660) you purchased from our Calverton showroom in January. We sincerely apologize for the inconvenience caused by the malfunctioning drying cycle and for the delay you experienced in reaching our service hotline.\n\nAfter reviewing your case, we have arranged the following. First, a certified technician will visit your home on Thursday, March 26, between 9:00 A.M. and noon, to replace the unit's heating element free of charge. Second, because the problem occurred within the ninety-day satisfaction period, we are extending your standard one-year warranty by an additional six months. Finally, as a gesture of goodwill, we have enclosed a $40 voucher that may be used toward any purchase at our showrooms or on our website.\n\nIf the repair does not fully resolve the issue, please contact me directly at 555-0126 rather than the general hotline, and we will arrange a replacement unit at no cost. We value your business and hope to serve you better in the future.\n\nSincerely,\n\nGrace Adeyemi\nCustomer Care Supervisor",
