    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All staff, Brennan Publishing House\nFrom: Theo Lindqvist, Sustainability Committee Chair\nDate: June 9\nSubject: Energy conservation measures, beginning July 1\n\nFollowing the board's approval of our sustainability plan last quarter, the following measures will take effect on July 1. Our goal is to reduce the building's electricity use by fifteen percent within one year.\n\n1. Lighting. Motion-activated sensors will be installed in all meeting rooms, storage areas, and restrooms during the last two weeks of June. Overhead lights in open work areas will switch off automatically at 8:00 P.M.; employees working later can turn them back on using the wall panels by the elevators.\n\n2. Equipment. All printers and copiers will enter sleep mode after ten minutes of inactivity. Staff are asked to shut down desktop computers at the end of each day rather than leaving them in standby. Laptops should be unplugged once fully charged.\n\n3. Climate control. From July through September, office temperatures will be set at 25°C, one degree higher than in previous summers. Personal electric fans are permitted; personal space heaters and coolers are not.\n\nThe committee will publish monthly updates on our intranet page showing the building's electricity consumption compared with last year. The department that achieves the largest reduction by December 31 will receive a catered lunch. Suggestions are welcome at sustainability@brennanpub.com.",
