    "question": "What is the purpose of the first passage?",
    "passage": "DINING OUT — A Bright Spot on Lakeside Avenue\nBy Renata Voss, Lakeside Gazette food critic\n\nSolstice Bistro has quietly become one of the most interesting tables in town. The seasonal menu, rebuilt every few months around local produce, is full of pleasant surprises, and the dessert list is simply outstanding — the honey-lavender cake alone is worth the trip. Much of the credit belongs to chef Marco Bell, who joined the bistro this spring. Still, the experience is not perfect. On both of my Saturday visits, service was noticeably slow, with long waits between courses. Parking is also a challenge, as the restaurant's small lot fills up quickly. Even so, Solstice Bistro earns a solid four stars out of five.\n\n--- Passage 2 ---\n\nTo: All Staff\nFrom: Hana Sato, Owner\nDate: November 3\nSubject: This week's review in the Gazette\n\nTeam,\n\nBy now many of you have seen Renata Voss's review of our bistro. Four stars is something to be proud of, and I want to especially thank our pastry team, whose work the critic singled out for praise. At the same time, we need to take the criticisms seriously. Starting next month, I am hiring two additional servers for Friday and Saturday evenings. Also beginning December 1, we will validate customer parking at the Grant Street garage, one block away, so guests will no longer need to depend on our small lot. Keep up the great work.\n\nHana",
