    "passage": "MEMO\nTo: All Hartwell Insurance employees\nFrom: Facilities Department\nDate: June 5\nRe: Headquarters relocation\n\nAs announced in April, our headquarters will move from Dale Street to Compton Tower over the weekend of June 27–28. All employees must pack the contents of their desks by the end of the day on Thursday, June 26. Boxes and labels may be picked up from the Facilities Department on the third floor. Do not pack your computer or monitors; the IT team will disconnect and reconnect all equipment. All staff will work remotely on Monday, June 29, and report to Compton Tower on Tuesday, June 30. The new building offers a fitness room and underground parking. Employees who wish to park on-site must apply for a permit by June 15.\n\n--- Passage 2 ---\n\nTo: facilities@hartwellins.com\nFrom: Rachel Imani <rimani@hartwellins.com>\nDate: June 10\nSubject: Moving questions\n\nHello,\n\nI have a few questions about the move. First, I stopped by the third floor yesterday afternoon to pick up labels, but the office was closed — could you tell me what hours someone will be there this week? Second, I would like to apply for an underground parking permit; please send me the application form. Finally, the memo says not to pack computers, but I also have a desk printer that belongs to my department. Should I pack it myself, or will the IT team handle it along with the computers?\n\nThank you,\nRachel Imani",
