    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "Why did Ms. Choi send the email?",
    "passage": "To: Marcus Bell <m.bell@torvilfasteners.com>\nFrom: Yuna Choi <y.choi@kestrelmotors.com>\nDate: April 17\nSubject: Quality concern — Order #KM-5582\n\nDear Mr. Bell,\n\nI am writing regarding the shipment of steel hinge brackets we received from Torvil Fasteners on April 14 (Order #KM-5582). During our routine incoming inspection, our quality team found that approximately 8 percent of the brackets in the batch fell outside the agreed thickness tolerance of 2.5 millimeters, plus or minus 0.1 millimeters. Under the terms of our supply agreement, the acceptable defect rate is no more than 2 percent.\n\nWe have set aside the nonconforming parts and can return them at your expense, or your technicians are welcome to examine them at our facility in Granton. Because these brackets are needed for an assembly run scheduled to start on April 28, we would ask that replacement parts be delivered no later than April 25.\n\nPlease also send a corrective action report describing how the issue occurred and what steps will be taken to prevent it. We value our four-year partnership with Torvil and trust this matter can be resolved quickly.\n\nSincerely,\nYuna Choi\nPurchasing Manager, Kestrel Motors",
