    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Assembly and Welding Personnel\nFrom: Dario Fontaine, Safety Compliance Officer\nDate: September 2\nSubject: Updated protective equipment requirements\n\nFollowing last month's safety audit, Brennan Metalworks is updating its personal protective equipment policy, effective September 15. The audit found that while compliance with hard hat and steel-toed boot requirements was excellent, eye protection practices were inconsistent, particularly in the welding bays.\n\nBeginning September 15, all personnel entering the welding bays—including visitors and office staff—must wear the new full-coverage safety goggles rather than standard safety glasses. The goggles will be distributed at the equipment counter starting September 8; please bring your employee badge to receive your pair. Prescription lens wearers should see Ms. Okada in Human Resources by September 5 so that fitted goggles can be ordered in time.\n\nIn addition, hearing protection will now be mandatory in the stamping area whenever the presses are in operation, not only during extended shifts as before. Disposable earplugs will remain available at all entrances, and reusable earmuffs may be requested from your supervisor.\n\nSupervisors will review the updated policy at next week's toolbox talks. Repeated noncompliance will be documented and may affect annual performance evaluations.",
