    "question": "Why was the shipment delayed?",
    "passage": "To: Helena Vargas <h.vargas@castellanohome.com>\nFrom: Customer Care <care@bluharborfreight.com>\nDate: November 19\nSubject: Update on shipment BHF-77241\n\nDear Ms. Vargas,\n\nWe are writing to inform you that shipment BHF-77241, containing forty cartons of ceramic tableware bound for your distribution center in Pemberton, has been delayed. The container vessel carrying your goods was rerouted because of severe weather in the Camden Strait and is now expected to dock at Port Reyes on November 24, three days later than originally scheduled.\n\nOnce the container clears customs, our ground team will deliver it to Pemberton within 48 hours. Based on current processing times at Port Reyes, we estimate arrival at your facility on November 27.\n\nWe recognize that this shipment contains seasonal merchandise, so we have upgraded the ground portion of the journey to our priority service at no additional charge. In addition, under the terms of your Silver Plan, you are entitled to a 15 percent credit on the shipping fee for any delivery delayed by more than 72 hours; the credit will appear on your December invoice automatically.\n\nYou can track the shipment in real time at www.bluharborfreight.com/track. Should you have questions, please reply to this email or call our service line at 555-0182.\n\nSincerely,\nBlu Harbor Freight Customer Care",
