    "id": "p7-0295",
    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What is the memo mainly about?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Warehouse Staff, Norvale Distribution Center\nFrom: Tomasz Krupa, Inventory Control Manager\nDate: January 8\nSubject: New cycle counting procedure\n\nStarting February 1, the Norvale Distribution Center will replace its annual full-facility inventory count with a cycle counting program. Instead of closing the warehouse for two days each December, small sections of inventory will be counted continuously throughout the year.\n\nUnder the new system, each aisle will be counted at least once per quarter. High-value items, such as electronics stored in the secured cage, will be counted monthly. Counts will take place during the first hour of the morning shift, before order picking begins, to minimize disruption.\n\nA team of six staff members will be designated as cycle counters on a rotating basis. Counters will use the handheld scanners already in use for receiving; a software update enabling the counting module will be installed on January 25. A mandatory forty-five-minute orientation will be held in the break room on January 28 at 8:00 A.M. and repeated at 2:30 P.M. for the afternoon shift.\n\nThis change should improve inventory accuracy, reduce year-end overtime costs, and help us identify discrepancies before they affect customer orders. Questions may be directed to me at extension 4471.",
    "options": [
      "A change in how inventory is counted",
      "The installation of new security cameras",
      "A reduction in warehouse operating hours",
      "The hiring of seasonal warehouse workers"
    ],
    "answer": 0,
    "explanation": "메모는 연 1회 전체 재고 조사를 연중 순환 실사(cycle counting) 방식으로 바꾼다는 내용을 중심으로 새 절차, 일정, 교육을 안내하고 있습니다. 보안 카메라, 운영 시간 단축, 계절 인력 채용은 언급되지 않았습니다.",
