    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What is the main purpose of the email?",
    "passage": "To: All Department Heads <dept-heads@meridianparts.com>\nFrom: Salome Diallo <s.diallo@meridianparts.com>\nDate: August 21\nSubject: New shipping carrier agreement\n\nDear Colleagues,\n\nAfter a three-month evaluation of bids from five carriers, Meridian Parts has signed a two-year agreement with Quickstone Logistics, effective October 1. Quickstone will handle all domestic ground shipments; international and overnight air shipments will continue to go through our current carrier, Aeroway Express.\n\nThe new agreement reduces our average domestic shipping cost by approximately 12 percent and includes guaranteed two-day delivery to customers within 800 kilometers of our warehouses. Quickstone will also provide a dedicated account representative and a daily pickup at 4:30 P.M., one hour later than our current cutoff, giving our order fulfillment team additional time to process late orders.\n\nTo prepare for the transition, the shipping department will hold brief demonstrations of Quickstone's online portal on September 24 and 26. Anyone who creates shipping labels or schedules pickups should attend one demonstration. Departments should also use up remaining preprinted forms from our former domestic carrier by September 30, as these cannot be used afterward.\n\nPlease share this information with your teams. A list of frequently asked questions will be posted on the company intranet next week.\n\nRegards,\nSalome Diallo\nDirector of Procurement",
