    "type": "RC",
    "question": "Why was the automated kiosk installed?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Delivery Drivers and Dock Personnel\nFrom: Ingrid Solberg, Terminal Operations Manager\nDate: May 12\nSubject: Revised check-in procedure at Gate 4\n\nEffective Monday, May 19, all inbound trucks at the Harwick Terminal must check in at the new automated kiosk at Gate 4. The kiosk replaces the paper sign-in sheets previously kept in the dispatch office and is intended to shorten wait times during the morning rush, when as many as thirty trucks arrive between 6:00 and 8:00 A.M.\n\nTo check in, drivers should scan the QR code on their delivery manifest, enter their trailer number, and select an available dock door from the on-screen list. The kiosk will print a dock assignment slip, which must be displayed on the dashboard while the vehicle is on terminal property. Drivers without a printed manifest can enter their booking reference manually, though this takes slightly longer.\n\nDock personnel should note that door assignments will now appear automatically on the warehouse display boards; radio confirmation from dispatch is no longer required, except for oversized loads and refrigerated trailers, which still need manual assignment.\n\nDuring the first two weeks, a dispatcher will be stationed at Gate 4 from 5:30 A.M. to 9:00 A.M. to assist drivers unfamiliar with the system. Comments about the new procedure may be left in the suggestion box outside the drivers' lounge.",
