    "type": "RC",
    "question": "Why was the email sent?",
    "passage": "To: Registered Patients <patients@cedarbrookclinic.org>\nFrom: Cedarbrook Family Clinic <noreply@cedarbrookclinic.org>\nDate: February 10\nSubject: Changes to our appointment reminder service\n\nDear Patients,\n\nBeginning March 1, Cedarbrook Family Clinic will switch to a new appointment reminder system called CareNotify. The current system, which sends a single phone call two days before each visit, will be retired at the end of February.\n\nWith CareNotify, you will receive a text message one week before your appointment and a second reminder 24 hours in advance. Each message contains a link allowing you to confirm, reschedule, or cancel without calling our front desk. Patients who prefer voice calls or who do not use a mobile phone can keep receiving telephone reminders by calling 555-0147 and selecting option 3 before February 25.\n\nPlease note that our cancellation policy remains unchanged: appointments canceled less than 24 hours in advance may be subject to a $30 fee, except in cases of emergency. We encourage you to use the rescheduling link as soon as you know you cannot attend, since same-week openings fill quickly, especially with Dr. Mehta and Dr. Russo, whose schedules are typically booked three weeks ahead.\n\nIf your mobile number has changed in the past year, please update it through the patient portal or at your next visit.\n\nWarm regards,\nCedarbrook Family Clinic Administration",
