    "id": "p7-0319",
    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "Why is the clinic adding Saturday hours?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Staff, Larkfield Community Clinic\nFrom: Renata Borges, Clinic Administrator\nDate: April 2\nSubject: Saturday hours beginning in May\n\nIn response to patient survey results showing strong demand for weekend availability, Larkfield Community Clinic will open on Saturdays from 9:00 A.M. to 1:00 P.M. beginning May 3. Saturday services will initially be limited to general consultations, vaccinations, and blood draws; specialist appointments and imaging will remain weekday-only for the time being.\n\nSaturday shifts will be staffed by two physicians, three nurses, and two front-desk employees on a rotating basis. Working one Saturday earns a half day of compensatory leave, which must be used within three months. The April rotation schedule will be posted in the staff lounge by April 11, and staff may swap assigned Saturdays with a colleague in the same role, provided both employees notify me by e-mail at least five days beforehand.\n\nThe pharmacy next door, Hartwell Drugs, has agreed to match our Saturday hours starting the same weekend, so patients can fill prescriptions immediately after their visits.\n\nWe will review appointment volumes at the end of July to decide whether to extend Saturday hours into the afternoon. Please direct questions to my office or raise them at the staff meeting on April 9.",
