    "question": "Why was the email sent to Voltcraft Electric?",
    "passage": "To: Estimating Department <estimating@voltcraftelectric.com>\nFrom: Hana Lindgren <h.lindgren@pinnaclebuildgroup.com>\nDate: January 22\nSubject: Invitation to bid — Maplewood Library renovation\n\nDear Voltcraft Electric,\n\nPinnacle Build Group has been selected as the general contractor for the renovation of the Maplewood Public Library, and we are inviting qualified subcontractors to submit bids for the electrical work. The scope includes replacing the main distribution panel, installing energy-efficient lighting throughout the 2,400-square-meter building, and wiring twelve new public computer stations on the second floor.\n\nBid documents, including drawings and specifications, can be downloaded from our contractor portal at www.pinnaclebuild.com/bids using access code MPL-2291. Sealed bids must be received at our Granview office no later than 3:00 P.M. on February 19. Bids arriving after this time will be returned unopened, without exception.\n\nA non-mandatory site walkthrough will be held on February 4 at 10:00 A.M.; while attendance is optional, contractors who have visited the site in past projects tell us it is helpful for estimating the conduit routing in the older wing. Please confirm attendance with our office by February 2 if you plan to join.\n\nNote that the library will remain open during construction, so the successful bidder must be able to schedule disruptive work outside public hours. Questions about the bid documents should be submitted in writing by February 12.\n\nSincerely,\nHana Lindgren\nProcurement Manager, Pinnacle Build Group",
