    "type": "RC",
    "question": "Why will Orchard Lane be closed?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Tenants and Site Crews, Orchard Lane Development\nFrom: Mateo Quintana, Construction Liaison\nDate: June 25\nSubject: Crane operations and temporary street closure, July 7–9\n\nPlease be advised that a 200-ton mobile crane will be on site from Monday, July 7, through Wednesday, July 9, to lift rooftop mechanical units onto Building B. To accommodate the crane and delivery trucks, the section of Orchard Lane between Vine Street and Cooper Road will be fully closed to vehicles from 7:00 A.M. to 6:00 P.M. on those three days. Pedestrian access along the east sidewalk will remain open at all times, with flaggers stationed at both ends of the closure.\n\nResidents of the adjacent Orchard Court apartments may park in the visitor lot at 48 Cooper Road free of charge during the closure; permits are available from the rental office until July 3. Business deliveries for the bakery and pharmacy on Vine Street should be redirected to the rear loading alley.\n\nLifting operations will pause if sustained winds exceed 38 kilometers per hour, in which case work will continue on the next suitable day, potentially extending the closure into Thursday. Updates will be posted each evening at www.orchardlanedev.com/traffic and on the notice board at the site entrance.\n\nWe appreciate your patience and apologize for any inconvenience. Direct questions to my office at 555-0166, extension 12.",
