    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What is the main purpose of the memo?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Instructors and Curriculum Staff\nFrom: Devraj Banerjee, Director of Learning Technology\nDate: November 3\nSubject: Rollout of the Skylark teaching platform\n\nStarting with the January term, Crestfield Professional Institute will deliver all course materials, assignments, and grades through the Skylark platform, replacing the three separate systems we currently use. Skylark was selected after a six-month pilot in the Business English department, where instructor feedback highlighted its simple grade entry and its mobile app, which most students in the pilot used daily.\n\nMigration of existing course content will be handled centrally by my team; instructors do not need to transfer their own files. However, each instructor must complete two steps before December 12: first, attend one ninety-minute hands-on workshop (offered every Tuesday and Thursday in November, both in person and online); second, log in to Skylark and verify that the migrated content of at least one current course is accurate. Any errors should be reported through the orange \"Flag content\" button rather than by email, as flagged items are routed directly to the migration team with all the necessary technical details attached.\n\nInstructors teaching evening classes may request a recorded version of the workshop, though the live sessions are strongly recommended because they include practice with the gradebook. Department coordinators will receive weekly completion reports throughout November.\n\nA student-facing introduction video will be sent to all enrolled learners during the first week of December.",
