    "type": "RC",
    "question": "Why can results NOT be provided by phone?",
    "passage": "To: Course Participants, Cohort 14 <cohort14@apexcert.com>\nFrom: Margit Halonen <m.halonen@apexcert.com>\nDate: December 2\nSubject: Examination results and next steps\n\nDear Participants,\n\nCongratulations on completing the Certified Logistics Analyst examination on November 21. Individual score reports were uploaded to your candidate accounts this morning; please sign in at www.apexcert.com/portal to view yours. For security reasons, results cannot be given over the phone or by email.\n\nOf the thirty-eight candidates in Cohort 14, thirty-one earned a passing score of 70 or above—the highest pass rate we have recorded in the program's nine years. Successful candidates will receive a printed certificate and a digital badge within three weeks. The digital badge can be added to professional networking profiles and verified by employers through our website.\n\nCandidates who did not pass may retake the examination once at half the standard fee, provided the retake occurs within six months of the original test date. A focused review course covering the two most challenging sections—customs documentation and freight cost analysis—will be offered online each Saturday in January. Enrollment is optional but strongly encouraged, as 85 percent of last year's retake candidates who completed the review course passed on their second attempt.\n\nFinally, please note that the certification is valid for three years. Renewal requires twenty hours of approved continuing education, which can be logged through the candidate portal at any time.\n\nBest regards,\nMargit Halonen\nCertification Programs Director, Apex Professional Certification",
