    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What will happen in June?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Machine Operators, Carverton Plant\nFrom: Henrik Dahl, Continuous Improvement Lead\nDate: February 17\nSubject: Suggestion program results and next round\n\nThank you to everyone who took part in the first round of the Bright Ideas suggestion program. Between October and January, operators submitted forty-seven improvement ideas, of which nine have been approved for implementation.\n\nThe top suggestion came from Ms. Paulina Reyes of the stamping department, who proposed storing die-change tools on shadow boards beside each press rather than in the central tool crib. Since the change was tested in January, average die changeover time has fallen from fifty-two minutes to thirty-four, and the layout will be extended to all presses by the end of March. Ms. Reyes will receive the $500 quarterly award, and her idea will be entered into the company-wide competition in June.\n\nOther approved suggestions include relocating the scrap bins to reduce forklift traffic in aisle 7 and adding a second label printer at packaging station 4, which often caused bottlenecks during peak runs.\n\nThe next submission round is open now through May 31. Ideas should be entered on the terminals in the break areas; handwritten forms are no longer accepted, as several were lost or illegible last round. Operators whose ideas are approved receive a $50 gift card in addition to eligibility for the quarterly award. Joint submissions from teams of up to four people are now welcome.\n\nKeep the ideas coming.",
