    "type": "RC",
    "question": "According to the memo, when is it still acceptable to call the yard office?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Field Crews, Tallis Brothers Construction\nFrom: Wendell Okafor, Equipment Manager\nDate: February 9\nSubject: New procedure for reserving heavy equipment\n\nEffective March 1, all requests for shared heavy equipment—excavators, skid steers, compactors, and the two boom lifts—must be made through the EquipTrack online system instead of by calling the yard office. Crew foremen received login credentials by email last week; anyone who has not received theirs should contact the IT help desk.\n\nUnder the new procedure, requests must be entered at least 48 hours before the equipment is needed. The system shows real-time availability, so foremen can immediately see open dates and avoid the double bookings that caused delays on at least four projects last year. Once a request is approved, EquipTrack sends a confirmation with the delivery window, and our yard drivers receive the haul schedule automatically.\n\nEmergency same-day requests will still be handled by phone, but please reserve this channel for genuine emergencies such as equipment breakdowns. Last-minute requests for poor planning reasons will be flagged, and repeat occurrences will be discussed at the monthly foremen's meeting.\n\nReturning equipment late affects other crews, so EquipTrack will also send a reminder the day before a scheduled return. If your project needs the machine longer, request an extension in the system; extensions are granted automatically unless another crew has reserved the unit.\n\nA fifteen-minute tutorial video is posted on the company intranet under \"Equipment.\"",
    "options": [
      "When requesting an extension",
      "When equipment breaks down unexpectedly",
      "When a foreman forgets his login credentials",
      "When confirming a delivery window"
    ],
    "answer": 1,
    "explanation": "'Emergency same-day requests will still be handled by phone, but please reserve this channel for genuine emergencies such as equipment breakdowns'라고 하여, 장비 고장 같은 진짜 비상시에만 전화 요청이 허용됩니다. 로그인 문제는 IT 헬프데스크, 연장 요청은 시스템을 통해야 합니다.",
    "difficulty": "medium"
