    "id": "p7-0403",
    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "Why are temperature records at concrete pours important, according to the email?",
    "passage": "To: All Site Supervisors <supervisors@crestlinebuilders.com>\nFrom: Olivia Marchetti <o.marchetti@crestlinebuilders.com>\nDate: November 12\nSubject: Winter weather protocols, effective December 1\n\nDear Supervisors,\n\nWith cold weather approaching, please review the winter protocols below, which apply to all Crestline sites from December 1 through March 15.\n\nConcrete work. Pouring is prohibited when the air temperature is below minus five degrees Celsius or expected to fall below that level within twenty-four hours of the pour, unless heated enclosures and insulating blankets are used. Supervisors must record the temperature at the time of each pour in the daily log; last winter, missing temperature records complicated a warranty claim on the Ashfield garage project and delayed its resolution by four months.\n\nWorker safety. When the wind chill drops below minus fifteen, outdoor crews must be offered a ten-minute warming break every hour in the heated site trailer. Sites without a trailer should contact facilities by November 21 to arrange one. Insulated gloves and thermal liners for hard hats will be shipped to each site by the end of next week at no cost to employees.\n\nSnow removal. Each site must designate a snow contractor by November 28 and post the contractor's emergency number in the site office. Access roads, scaffold platforms, and walkways must be cleared and salted before crews begin work, and any delay caused by snow clearing should be coded as weather time, not productive hours, in the timesheet system.\n\nThe full protocol document is on the company portal under Safety > Seasonal. Confirm by reply that your site is prepared.\n\nRegards,\nOlivia Marchetti\nRegional Operations Manager",
    "options": [
      "Missing records once slowed down a warranty claim.",
      "They are required for workers' overtime pay.",
      "Inspectors collect them every December.",
      "They determine the price of concrete."
    ],
    "answer": 0,
    "explanation": "'last winter, missing temperature records complicated a warranty claim on the Ashfield garage project and delayed its resolution by four months'라고 하여, 작년에 온도 기록 누락으로 하자보증 처리에 4개월의 지연이 발생했기 때문에 기록이 중요함을 강조하고 있습니다.",
    "difficulty": "medium"
