    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What is suggested about the cost of the substitute blocks?",
    "passage": "To: Hollis Park Project Team <hollispark@dunmorecivil.com>\nFrom: Tobias Reinholt <t.reinholt@dunmorecivil.com>\nDate: May 30\nSubject: Material substitution approval — retaining wall blocks\n\nDear Team,\n\nThis email confirms the outcome of yesterday's discussion with the client and the structural engineer regarding the retaining wall along the eastern edge of the Hollis Park site.\n\nAs you know, our specified supplier, Keystone Precast, notified us on May 22 that the approved W-40 wall blocks are backordered until mid-August because of a kiln failure at their plant. Waiting would push the wall completion past the July 31 milestone, which carries a contractual penalty of $1,200 per day. We therefore requested approval to substitute the V-38 block from Borchert Concrete Products, which is available for delivery within two weeks.\n\nThe structural engineer has now reviewed Borchert's test certificates and confirmed the V-38 meets or exceeds the specified compressive strength and freeze-thaw durability ratings. The client signed the substitution form this morning, with one condition: because the V-38 has a slightly different surface texture, a sample panel of at least two square meters must be built and photographed for the client's records before full installation begins. Mr. Castellanos, please schedule this panel for the week of June 9 and invite the client's representative to view it in person.\n\nThe substitution saves us from the delay penalty, and Borchert's unit price is actually 3 percent lower, though increased delivery distance will absorb most of that difference. Please update the procurement log and the as-built drawings accordingly.\n\nRegards,\nTobias Reinholt\nProject Manager, Dunmore Civil Engineering",
    "options": [
      "The savings will mostly be offset by delivery costs.",
      "They are significantly more expensive than the originals.",
      "The client will pay the price difference.",
      "Borchert is offering them free of charge."
    ],
    "answer": 0,
    "explanation": "'Borchert's unit price is actually 3 percent lower, though increased delivery distance will absorb most of that difference'라고 되어 있어, 단가는 3퍼센트 저렴하지만 늘어난 운송 거리 비용이 그 절감분의 대부분을 상쇄할 것임을 알 수 있습니다.",
