    "passage": "Aisha Konadu (10:05 A.M.)\nMr. Veltri, this is Aisha Konadu from Lakeshore Apparel. I'm reviewing the embroidery samples you sent for our staff polo shirts. The stitching quality is excellent, but the navy thread looks lighter than our brand color.\n\nGiorgio Veltri (10:12 A.M.)\nThank you for the close look, Ms. Konadu. We matched thread to the color code in your March style guide — PMS 2965. Has the guide changed?\n\nAisha Konadu (10:15 A.M.)\nAh, that explains it. We updated to PMS 2767 in April. The newer guide must not have reached you. I'll send it now.\n\nGiorgio Veltri (10:18 A.M.)\nReceived. We stock 2767 thread, so no special order needed. New samples can ship Wednesday. However, I should mention our production calendar: to deliver all 600 shirts by July 1, we need final sample approval by June 16.\n\nAisha Konadu (10:21 A.M.)\nThat's only two days after the new samples would arrive. Our approval process normally routes through three department heads.\n\nGiorgio Veltri (10:24 A.M.)\nWe could send digital photos of the corrected samples Monday, ahead of the physical shipment. Many clients pre-approve from photos and confirm on receipt.\n\nAisha Konadu (10:26 A.M.)\nThat could shave off the wait. I'll ask the department heads to review photos Monday afternoon and treat the physical samples as final confirmation only.\n\nGiorgio Veltri (10:28 A.M.)\nExcellent. I'll note the conditional approval process on your order file and send the photos by 9:00 A.M. Monday.",
