    "passage": "Leandro Costa (9:40 A.M.)\nMs. Thornton, Leandro from Costa Tile here. We pulled up the old flooring in your café's entryway this morning and found the subfloor underneath is water-damaged in spots. About four square meters need replacing.\n\nBeverly Thornton (9:52 A.M.)\nI was afraid of something like that. How does this affect the price and schedule?\n\nLeandro Costa (9:55 A.M.)\nMaterials and labor for the subfloor add $620. Time-wise, it adds one day — we'd finish Thursday instead of Wednesday.\n\nBeverly Thornton (9:58 A.M.)\nMy reopening ad in the Weekend Courier already says \"Friday.\" Does Thursday completion truly leave enough margin?\n\nLeandro Costa (10:02 A.M.)\nThe tile needs 24 hours before heavy foot traffic, so a Thursday afternoon finish means Friday evening opening at the earliest. Morning would be pushing it.\n\nBeverly Thornton (10:05 A.M.)\nThe ad says doors open at 7:00 A.M. That won't fly.\n\nLeandro Costa (10:08 A.M.)\nThere's another route: we can use a rapid-set mortar that's ready for traffic in three hours. It costs $180 more, but you'd open Friday morning with time to spare.\n\nBeverly Thornton (10:11 A.M.)\nBetween reprinting ads and losing my opening morning, $180 is the cheapest problem I've heard all day. Go with the rapid-set.\n\nLeandro Costa (10:13 A.M.)\nWill do. I'll send the revised work order — $800 total in additions — for your signature this afternoon.",
