    "passage": "Library Renovation Chat\n\nFatima El-Sayed (1:30 P.M.)\nCommittee, the contractor confirmed the children's wing will be ready August 4, two weeks earlier than planned. Should we move the reopening celebration up as well?\n\nBruce Hollings (1:34 P.M.)\nTempting, but our headline performer — the puppet theater troupe — is booked solid until August 18, our original date.\n\nNadine Toussaint (1:36 P.M.)\nAnd the commemorative bookmarks won't arrive until the 15th. The printer needed six weeks because of the gold foil.\n\nFatima El-Sayed (1:39 P.M.)\nFair points. But an empty, finished wing for two weeks seems like a missed opportunity. Ideas?\n\nBruce Hollings (1:42 P.M.)\nA \"soft opening\" — open the wing quietly on the 4th for regular library hours, then hold the full celebration on the 18th as planned. Schools are still out, so kids would use it right away.\n\nNadine Toussaint (1:45 P.M.)\nI like it. We could even use the soft-opening period to spot any problems — like whether the new shelving height works for the picture-book section — before the big day brings crowds and press.\n\nFatima El-Sayed (1:48 P.M.)\nA built-in trial run. Bruce, would the troupe consider adding a smaller weekday show during those two weeks? Even thirty minutes?\n\nBruce Hollings (1:51 P.M.)\nTheir Tuesday mornings looked open when we first talked. I'll ask about August 12 and report back by tomorrow.\n\nFatima El-Sayed (1:53 P.M.)\nPerfect. Nadine, let's also draft a simple flyer for the soft opening — nothing fancy, just dates and hours.",
