    "passage": "Yara Haddad (4:10 P.M.)\nHi Mr. Brennan, this is Yara from Pixel & Co. About the product photography for your kayak line — I've reviewed the brief. You'd like 60 studio shots and an outdoor session at Mirror Lake, correct?\n\nConnor Brennan (4:18 P.M.)\nThat's right. The catalog deadline is July 10, and our marketing lead wants golden-hour lighting for the lake shots.\n\nYara Haddad (4:21 P.M.)\nGolden hour at Mirror Lake in late June means roughly 7:40 to 8:30 P.M. I should flag one thing: the lake's north shore — the one with the mountain backdrop from your reference photos — requires a commercial filming permit from the county.\n\nConnor Brennan (4:25 P.M.)\nI had no idea. How long does that take?\n\nYara Haddad (4:27 P.M.)\nTen business days, typically. If we apply by this Friday, we're covered for a June 25 or 26 shoot, with the 27th as a weather backup.\n\nConnor Brennan (4:30 P.M.)\nLet's not gamble with the catalog. Apply today if possible. What do you need from me?\n\nYara Haddad (4:33 P.M.)\nA signed letter authorizing me to act as your agent, plus the $150 permit fee — both can be done electronically. I'll send the forms within the hour.\n\nConnor Brennan (4:36 P.M.)\nI'll watch for them. And the studio shots — can those happen while we wait on the permit?\n\nYara Haddad (4:38 P.M.)\nExactly my plan. My studio is open June 17 and 18. Ship me three kayaks and the paddle accessories by the 16th, and we'll have the studio half wrapped before the lake session.",
