    "question": "What is the main purpose of the article?",
    "passage": "HARLOW VALLEY (June 2) — Brightbean Coffee, the popular café chain headquartered in Marston, announced yesterday that it will open twelve new locations across the Harlow Valley region over the next eighteen months. The expansion, the company's largest to date, is expected to create approximately 240 jobs, including baristas, shift supervisors, and regional managers.\n\n\"Harlow Valley has experienced remarkable population growth in recent years, and we believe the area can sustain a strong demand for specialty coffee,\" said Priya Raman, Brightbean's chief operating officer. \"We have been studying this market for nearly three years, and the timing is finally right.\"\n\nThe first two cafés will open in downtown Eastwick and at the Harlow Valley Shopping Centre in September. Unlike the chain's existing stores, the new locations will feature an expanded food menu developed in partnership with local bakery Crowfield Ovens. Ms. Raman noted that sourcing pastries locally would reduce delivery distances and support neighborhood businesses.\n\nBrightbean currently operates 85 cafés in four regions. Industry analyst Tomas Greer called the move \"a calculated risk,\" pointing out that two competing chains already have a solid footing in the valley. Nevertheless, Brightbean's stock rose three percent following the announcement.",
