    "question": "What does Mr. Adeyemi indicate about the Cargomax E1?",
    "passage": "FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\nVeltron Motors Unveils All-Electric Delivery Van\n\nDARROWFIELD (April 8) — Veltron Motors today introduced the Cargomax E1, the company's first fully electric delivery van, at the Darrowfield Commercial Vehicle Show. Designed for urban courier services and grocery retailers, the Cargomax E1 can travel up to 310 kilometers on a single charge and recharges to 80 percent capacity in under 40 minutes at a fast-charging station.\n\n\"Delivery fleets account for a substantial portion of city traffic, so electrifying them has an immediate effect on air quality,\" said Veltron's head of product development, Marcus Adeyemi. \"We built the E1 from the ground up rather than converting an existing model, which allowed us to maximize cargo space.\"\n\nThe van's interior offers 11 cubic meters of storage and a low loading floor that reduces strain on drivers who make frequent stops. Veltron has already secured orders from two national parcel carriers, and the company expects to deliver the first 500 vehicles by January.\n\nPricing starts at $52,000, though buyers in many regions will qualify for government incentives that lower the effective cost. Production will take place at Veltron's recently modernized plant in Ostbrook, where the company has hired 150 additional assembly workers.",
