    "passage": "STRATHMOOR (February 19) — Strathmoor Regional Airport unveiled plans on Tuesday for a $310 million expansion that officials say will nearly double the airport's passenger capacity by 2029. The project's centerpiece is a new concourse with twelve additional gates, but it also includes a larger baggage-handling facility, 2,000 more parking spaces, and a consolidated security checkpoint designed to cut average wait times in half.\n\nPassenger traffic at Strathmoor has grown 46 percent over the past five years, driven largely by the arrival of two low-cost carriers and the region's expanding convention business. Airport director Samuel Ito said the existing terminal, built in 1988, was designed to handle four million passengers annually but served nearly seven million last year. \"Travelers feel the strain at every step, from curbside drop-off to boarding,\" Mr. Ito said. \"This expansion addresses the entire journey.\"\n\nConstruction will be carried out in phases to keep the airport fully operational. The parking garage will be built first, beginning this summer, followed by the concourse in early 2027. Funding will come from airport revenue bonds and passenger facility charges rather than local taxes, a point officials emphasized repeatedly at Tuesday's briefing.\n\nThe regional carrier Avelora Airlines has already announced that it will base four additional aircraft at Strathmoor once the new gates open, adding nonstop routes to six cities.",
