    "passage": "MERRIDALE (September 8) — Fennimore Markets, the grocery chain with 31 stores across the Merridale region, will begin offering home delivery next month, the company said Thursday. — [1] —. Customers will be able to place orders through a new mobile application or the company's website, with deliveries promised within two hours for orders placed before 6:00 P.M.\n\nThe service will launch first in the cities of Merridale and Okosa on October 6, with the remaining service areas added by the end of the year. — [2] —. Delivery will be free for orders over $60; smaller orders will carry a $5.99 fee.\n\nTo support the program, Fennimore has converted a warehouse on Quarry Road into a fulfillment center where workers assemble online orders. — [3] —. The company has hired 85 drivers and plans to operate a fleet of refrigerated vans to keep produce, dairy, and frozen items at safe temperatures during transport.\n\nFennimore's move comes as competition in the regional grocery business intensifies. — [4] —. Retail analyst Joon-ho Park noted that the chain's main rival, Belden Foods, has offered delivery for two years. \"Fennimore is late to this market, but its loyal customer base and dense store network could help it catch up quickly,\" Mr. Park said.",
