    "question": "What is the press release mainly about?",
    "passage": "FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\nHaldane Pharmaceuticals Breaks Ground on Research Campus\n\nNORWICK (March 12) — Haldane Pharmaceuticals held a groundbreaking ceremony yesterday for its new research and development campus on the eastern edge of Norwick. The 28-hectare site will eventually house four laboratory buildings, a pilot manufacturing plant, and a conference center, representing a total investment of $480 million.\n\nThe first phase, consisting of two laboratories and the manufacturing plant, is scheduled to open in the autumn of next year. About 400 scientists and technicians currently working at Haldane's aging facility in Brockhurst will transfer to the campus, and the company expects to create 250 new research positions over the following three years.\n\n\"Our Brockhurst labs served us well for four decades, but modern drug development demands flexible spaces and specialized equipment that the old buildings simply cannot accommodate,\" said chief scientific officer Dr. Ingrid Vasquez. \"The Norwick campus is designed to be reconfigured as our research priorities evolve.\"\n\nHaldane selected Norwick after an eighteen-month search that considered sites in three countries. Company officials cited the proximity of Norwick University, whose graduate programs in chemistry and biology are highly regarded, as the deciding factor. The university and Haldane have also signed an agreement establishing paid internships for up to 30 graduate students each year at the new campus.",
