    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What is the article mainly about?",
    "passage": "DELLBROOK (June 14) — After twenty-six years at the corner of Asher Street and Vine Avenue, the Dellbrook Farmers' Market will move to a larger site at Copperfield Commons beginning the first weekend of July, market organizers announced this week.\n\nThe move has been under discussion for more than a year. The market has grown from a dozen stalls to more than ninety, and on busy Saturdays the narrow Asher Street site forced organizers to turn away as many as twenty vendors. The new location, a paved plaza beside the renovated Copperfield train station, offers nearly three times the space, sheltered areas for use in bad weather, and direct access to public transportation.\n\n\"Our waiting list of farmers and food producers has never been longer,\" said market manager Yusuf Demir. \"At Copperfield we can welcome them all, add a dedicated area for prepared-food trucks, and still have room for seating where people can actually enjoy what they buy.\"\n\nSome longtime customers have expressed sadness about leaving the original location, which many credit with revitalizing the Asher Street shopping district in the early 2000s. Mr. Demir acknowledged the attachment but noted that the market's lease was due to expire in August and that the property owner plans to construct an apartment building on the site. The market will continue to operate every Saturday from 8:00 A.M. to 1:00 P.M., and a free shuttle will run from Asher Street to Copperfield Commons during July.",
