    "question": "What is the purpose of the press release?",
    "passage": "FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\nCarmody Savings Bank Launches Mobile Banking App for Small Businesses\n\nLERWICK (October 22) — Carmody Savings Bank today released Carmody Biz, a mobile application created specifically for the bank's small-business customers. The app allows business owners to deposit checks remotely, schedule payments to suppliers, track spending by category, and grant limited account access to bookkeepers or business partners.\n\nThe bank developed the app over fourteen months in consultation with an advisory panel of thirty local business owners, who tested early versions and suggested refinements. \"Our panel told us that existing banking apps were built for individuals first, with business tools added as an afterthought,\" said Vera Kowalski, Carmody's director of digital services. \"We reversed that approach and designed every screen around how a business actually operates.\"\n\nOne feature that emerged directly from the panel's feedback is the app's invoice tool, which lets users create and send invoices and then matches incoming payments to them automatically. Panel member Dario Fuentes, who owns a landscaping company in Lerwick, said the feature has already saved him several hours of bookkeeping each week.\n\nCarmody Biz is available at no cost to any Carmody business account holder. The bank, which operates nineteen branches across the Lerwick area, said it will add payroll functions to the app early next year. Customers can register for a free online demonstration session through the bank's website.",
