    "question": "What is Pagewell Books planning to do next year?",
    "passage": "FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\nPagewell Books Marks 40th Anniversary with Expansion into Three Cities\n\nROSSDALE (August 5) — Pagewell Books, the independent bookstore chain founded in Rossdale in 1986, announced today that it will celebrate its fortieth anniversary by opening stores in Kelmore, Branton Hills, and Verity Springs next year, the company's first new locations in over a decade.\n\nEach new store will follow the format Pagewell introduced when it remodeled its flagship Rossdale shop four years ago: a carefully selected inventory of about 20,000 titles, a café serving coffee from local roasters, and an events space hosting author readings, book clubs, and children's story hours. That remodeling, initially questioned by some observers, increased the flagship store's sales by 31 percent in two years and is widely credited with reviving the company's fortunes.\n\n\"People predicted the end of physical bookstores for years, but our customers keep proving otherwise,\" said Pagewell president Nora Castellan, granddaughter of founder Arthur Pagewell. \"What readers want is a place that feels personal. You cannot download a conversation about a novel you loved.\"\n\nThe company will hire about 25 employees for each location, with store managers recruited internally from existing branches. Hiring for the remaining positions will begin in January through the careers page of the Pagewell website. The Kelmore store is scheduled to open in May, followed by Branton Hills in August and Verity Springs in November.",
