    "id": "p7-0719",
    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What is new at this year's festival?",
    "passage": "THE 28TH ANNUAL MAPLEBROOK HARVEST FESTIVAL\nSaturday, October 18 & Sunday, October 19 — Riverside Fairgrounds, Maplebrook\n\nCelebrate autumn at the region's favorite family event! This year's festival features over 90 local vendors selling crafts, preserves, and baked goods, plus a farmers' market, pumpkin carving contests, hayrides, and live music on two stages.\n\nNew this year: the Cider House Pavilion, where six area orchards will offer tastings from noon to 5:00 P.M. each day. Tasting wristbands are $12 and are limited to visitors aged 19 and over with valid photo identification.\n\nAdmission: Adults $8; children 12 and under free; seniors 65+ free on Sunday only. Parking at the fairgrounds is $5 per vehicle, but a complimentary shuttle runs every 20 minutes from the Maplebrook Transit Center for those who prefer to leave their cars at home.\n\nGates open at 10:00 A.M. both days. The festival closes at 8:00 P.M. on Saturday and 6:00 P.M. on Sunday. Rain or shine — most attractions are under cover. Pets, outside food, and personal coolers are not permitted on the fairgrounds.\n\nFull schedule at www.maplebrookharvestfest.org.",
