    "id": "p7-0723",
    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "How long does the festival last?",
    "passage": "www.coastlandlanternfest.org/visit\n\nCOASTLAND LANTERN FESTIVAL — VISITOR INFORMATION\n\nThe Coastland Lantern Festival returns to Harborview Park for three evenings, August 7 to 9, from 6:00 P.M. to 11:00 P.M. Wander among more than 300 illuminated lantern sculptures, enjoy performances by regional dance troupes, and sample dishes from 25 food trucks along the waterfront promenade.\n\nTickets: Advance tickets are $14 online and must be purchased for a specific evening. A limited number of gate tickets are sold each night for $18, but availability is not guaranteed — Friday and Saturday evenings sold out completely last year. Children under 5 enter free. A three-night pass is available online only for $30.\n\nAccessibility: All pathways are paved and wheelchair accessible. Wheelchairs may be borrowed free of charge at the information tent with a photo ID; quantities are limited and reservations are not accepted.\n\nGetting here: Parking near the park is extremely limited. We strongly encourage visitors to use the free festival ferry, which departs from the Brockton City Pier every 30 minutes starting at 5:30 P.M. The last return ferry leaves the park at 11:45 P.M.\n\nLantern artists interested in exhibiting next year may submit proposals through our Artists page between September 1 and October 31.",
