    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What is included with the food vendor space?",
    "passage": "MAPLEBROOK HARVEST FESTIVAL — VENDOR BOOTH APPLICATION\n\nThank you for your interest in selling at the 28th Annual Maplebrook Harvest Festival, October 18-19, at Riverside Fairgrounds.\n\nBooth Options (both days included):\n- Standard booth (3m x 3m): $150\n- Corner booth (3m x 3m, two open sides): $210\n- Food vendor space (includes electrical hookup): $325\n\nApplication Checklist:\n1. Completed application form\n2. Three photographs of your products or menu items\n3. A copy of your vendor liability insurance certificate\n4. Food vendors only: a valid county health permit\n\nApplications must be received by August 15. Because the festival favors handmade and locally produced goods, mass-produced merchandise will not be approved. Returning vendors in good standing receive priority placement but must still apply by the deadline.\n\nAccepted vendors will be notified by e-mail no later than September 1, and booth fees are due within 14 days of acceptance. Fees are refundable until September 20, minus a $25 processing charge; no refunds will be issued after that date for any reason, including weather, as the festival takes place rain or shine.\n\nQuestions? Contact the vendor coordinator at vendors@maplebrookharvestfest.org.",
