    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What will the Move Coordinator do?",
    "passage": "www.harborlinerelocations.com/jobs/dispatcher\n\nJOB OPENING: MOVE COORDINATOR / DISPATCHER — HARBORLINE RELOCATIONS, DELMONT OFFICE\n\nHarborline Relocations seeks an organized, calm-under-pressure Move Coordinator to schedule crews and serve as the main point of contact for customers on moving day.\n\nKey Duties:\n- Assign crews and trucks to daily jobs and adjust schedules when delays occur\n- Confirm move details with customers 48 hours in advance\n- Track crew arrival times and update customers throughout the day\n- Prepare end-of-day reports for the operations manager\n\nQualifications: a high school diploma, at least one year of dispatch, logistics, or customer service experience, and strong skills with scheduling software. Knowledge of the Delmont road network is helpful. This is an office-based position; no lifting or driving is involved.\n\nSchedule and Pay: Full-time, Tuesday through Saturday, 7:00 A.M. to 3:00 P.M. Starting pay is $21 per hour, with health benefits beginning after 60 days and two weeks of paid vacation per year. Note that during the peak season of June through September, coordinators are expected to remain on call one evening per week.\n\nE-mail your résumé to hiring@harborlinerelocations.com with \"Move Coordinator\" in the subject line. Applications close on April 4. No phone inquiries, please.",
