    "question": "What is the main purpose of the webpage?",
    "passage": "www.metroapplianceacademy.com/program\n\nBECOME A CERTIFIED APPLIANCE REPAIR TECHNICIAN — METRO APPLIANCE ACADEMY\n\nThe demand for skilled appliance technicians has never been higher. Metro Appliance Academy's 16-week certificate program prepares you for a stable, well-paid career — no prior experience needed.\n\nProgram Overview:\nStudents train hands-on in our fully equipped workshop, learning to diagnose and repair refrigerators, washers, dryers, dishwashers, and electric ranges. The curriculum also covers electrical safety, customer communication, and how to estimate repair costs. In the final four weeks, every student completes a paid apprenticeship with one of our twelve partner repair companies.\n\nClasses are offered in two tracks: a daytime track (Monday-Thursday, 9:00 A.M.-2:00 P.M.) and an evening track (Monday-Wednesday, 6:00 P.M.-9:30 P.M.). The evening track takes 20 weeks instead of 16 due to its reduced weekly hours.\n\nTuition is $4,900, including tools, safety equipment, and certification exam fees. Payment plans are available with no interest, and graduates who join a partner company receive a $500 tuition rebate after 90 days of employment.\n\nThe next daytime cohort begins September 8; the evening cohort begins September 15. Enrollment is limited to 18 students per cohort. Attend a free information session on August 20 to tour the workshop and meet instructors.",
