    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Sales Agents, Lakemont Mutual Insurance\nFrom: Gerald Pinsky, Vice President of Sales\nDate: November 2\nRe: New Policy Renewal Procedure\n\nEffective December 1, Lakemont Mutual will move from paper-based renewal notices to an automated digital renewal system for all auto and homeowner policies.\n\nUnder the new system, policyholders will receive a renewal offer by e-mail sixty days before their policy expires, followed by a reminder at thirty days. Customers who take no action will be renewed automatically at the quoted rate, provided their payment method on file is valid. Customers without an e-mail address on record will continue to receive printed notices by mail, so no policyholder will be left uninformed.\n\nWhat this means for you: agents will no longer need to generate renewal letters manually, a task that consumed roughly six hours per agent each week. Instead, you are expected to use that time for outreach calls to clients whose premiums will increase by more than ten percent at renewal, as these accounts carry the highest risk of cancellation. A list of such accounts will appear on your dashboard every Monday.\n\nTraining webinars will run November 17-19. Recordings will be available for those unable to attend live.",
