    "id": "p7-1077",
    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What is the purpose of the e-mail?",
    "passage": "To: All Field Agents, Northern Region\nFrom: Carla Jimenez <c.jimenez@beaconrockinsurance.com>\nSubject: Registration Open — Claims Technology Workshop, August 21\nDate: July 28\n\nDear Colleagues,\n\nRegistration is now open for our one-day workshop, Streamlining Claims with Mobile Tools, to be held on Thursday, August 21, at the Fairhaven Conference Center.\n\nThe workshop will introduce the new BeaconSnap mobile application, which allows agents to photograph damage, record customer statements, and submit complete claim files from the field. Agents who adopted the app during our spring pilot program reduced average claim-processing time from nine days to four. The morning session covers app navigation and photo standards; the afternoon session features hands-on practice with simulated claim scenarios.\n\nSpace is limited to forty participants, and spots will be assigned in the order registrations are received. Last year's session filled within a week, so early registration is strongly encouraged. To register, complete the form on the staff intranet under Training and Events no later than August 8. Lunch will be provided; please indicate any dietary restrictions on the form.\n\nAgents who complete the workshop will receive six continuing-education credits toward their license renewal.\n\nRegards,\nCarla Jimenez\nRegional Training Coordinator",
