    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What is the main purpose of the memo?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: Editorial and Production Staff, Quillstone Publishing\nFrom: Marianne Duval, Production Director\nDate: June 4\nRe: Consolidated E-book Conversion Workflow\n\nStarting July 1, all e-book conversion work will be handled in-house by our new digital production unit rather than by outside vendors. This change follows a six-month trial in which the unit converted eighteen titles with a forty percent reduction in per-title costs and an average turnaround of eight days, compared with the three weeks our vendors typically required.\n\nTo make the workflow run smoothly, editors must now submit final, approved manuscripts through the ProjectHub system instead of e-mailing files directly to production staff. Each submission must include the completed metadata form — title, contributor names, price category, and territorial rights — since incomplete forms were the leading cause of delays during the trial.\n\nPlease be aware that illustrated children's titles and cookbooks with complex layouts will continue to be sent to Pixelcraft Studio for the remainder of the year, as these formats require specialized fixed-layout conversion.\n\nA step-by-step guide to ProjectHub submissions is available on the intranet. Questions may be directed to Felix Arno at extension 2280.",
