    "question": "What is suggested about last year's booth?",
    "passage": "To: Exhibits Team <exhibits@meridianbooks.com>\nFrom: Howard Lassiter <h.lassiter@meridianbooks.com>\nSubject: Westhaven Book Fair — Booth Logistics\nDate: October 2\n\nTeam,\n\nWith the Westhaven International Book Fair three weeks away, here is an update on our arrangements.\n\nWe have secured booth 214, a corner location near the main entrance, which should give us considerably more foot traffic than last year's spot at the back of Hall C. The booth measures four meters by six meters, large enough for two display walls and a small signing table.\n\nOur freight carrier will collect display materials and book cartons from the warehouse on October 16. Anything not packed and labeled by 3:00 P.M. that day will have to be transported in personal vehicles, which our insurance does not cover, so please finish packing on time. Label every carton with the booth number and a contents list.\n\nThree author signings are confirmed: Lucia Ferrante on Friday at 2:00 P.M., and Devon Park and Amara Osei on Saturday. Friday afternoon is traditionally the fair's busiest period, so we expect long lines and will need at least four staff members at the booth then.\n\nPlease send me your preferred shifts by October 9.\n\nThanks,\nHoward",
