    "type": "RC",
    "question": "Why was the memo distributed?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Laboratory Personnel, Building 4\nFrom: Dr. Ingrid Vasquez, Director of Quality and Compliance\nDate: May 12\nRe: Preparation for Regulatory Safety Audit\n\nVireon Pharmaceuticals will undergo a scheduled safety audit by the National Health Authority during the week of June 2. Inspectors will examine laboratory practices, documentation, and storage conditions in Building 4. Please review the following requirements before the end of May.\n\nAll reagent containers must carry labels showing contents, concentration, receipt date, and expiration date. During last year's internal review, unlabeled secondary containers were our most frequently cited issue, and inspectors treat repeat findings severely.\n\nLaboratory notebooks must be completed in ink, signed, and dated on each page. Any unused space on a page should be crossed out. Equipment calibration records for balances, pH meters, and refrigerators must be current; if you notice an overdue calibration sticker, notify the metrology team immediately rather than using the instrument.\n\nFinally, the cold-storage units on the third floor will be reorganized on May 23, and access will be restricted that day. Plan your sample retrievals accordingly.\n\nA mock inspection will be conducted by my team on May 27. Findings will be shared with supervisors the following morning so corrections can be made before the actual audit.",
