    "question": "What is the purpose of the e-mail?",
    "passage": "To: Clinical Operations Team\nFrom: Dr. Samuel Adeyemi <s.adeyemi@calyxbiopharma.com>\nSubject: Recruitment Update — CLX-204 Trial\nDate: August 18\n\nDear Team,\n\nHere is the mid-quarter update on participant recruitment for the CLX-204 hypertension study.\n\nAs of August 15, we have enrolled 312 of the 450 participants required across our five study sites. The Brookfield and Santa Rosa clinics have already met their individual targets, while the Davenport site has reached only forty percent of its goal. Our analysis suggests the shortfall stems from the site's limited evening hours, which make visits difficult for working adults — the demographic most represented in our screening pool.\n\nTo address this, the Davenport clinic will begin offering appointments until 8:00 P.M. on Tuesdays and Thursdays starting September 1. In addition, we have received ethics board approval to place recruitment notices in three regional newspapers and on two transit lines. Updated flyers are attached; please discard earlier versions, which list an incorrect phone number for the screening office.\n\nIf enrollment does not reach 400 by October 31, we will need to discuss extending the recruitment window with the study sponsor, which could delay the interim analysis. Let's make every effort to avoid that outcome.\n\nBest,\nSamuel",
