    "type": "RC",
    "question": "Why is line 3 being converted?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: Packaging Department, Second Shift\nFrom: Hannah Strickland, Plant Operations Manager\nDate: January 20\nRe: Line 3 Changeover to Blister Packaging\n\nBeginning February 9, packaging line 3 will be converted from bottle filling to blister-pack production to support the launch of our new allergy tablet, Clarivex. The conversion addresses growing pharmacy demand for calendar-style packs, which help patients track daily doses.\n\nThe changeover will take place over two weekends, February 7-8 and February 14-15, so weekday production will not be interrupted. During this period, bottle-filling volume will shift temporarily to lines 1 and 2, and overtime slots will be available for operators willing to support the increased load. Sign-up sheets are posted outside the shift office.\n\nAll second-shift operators assigned to line 3 must complete a certification course on the new equipment before February 9. The course consists of a two-hour online module followed by a practical assessment conducted by the equipment manufacturer's trainer, who will be on site February 2-6. Operators who do not obtain certification by the deadline will be reassigned to other lines until they complete it.\n\nQuality assurance staff will run validation batches during the week of February 16; commercial production is scheduled to begin February 23.",
