    "question": "Why will electricity service be interrupted on March 28?",
    "passage": "To: Residential Customers, Glenbrook Service Area\nFrom: Tarrow Electric Cooperative <notices@tarrowelectric.com>\nSubject: Planned Power Interruption — Saturday, March 28\nDate: March 16\n\nDear Customer,\n\nTo replace aging transformers and install storm-resistant poles along Route 9, Tarrow Electric will interrupt service to the Glenbrook area on Saturday, March 28, from 8:00 A.M. to approximately 2:00 P.M.\n\nThis upgrade is part of our three-year grid modernization program, which has already reduced weather-related outages by thirty percent in the neighboring Pinehurst district. Once the work is complete, Glenbrook customers should experience fewer and shorter interruptions during severe weather.\n\nWe schedule planned work on weekends to minimize disruption to home-based businesses; however, we recognize that any outage is inconvenient. Customers who rely on electrically powered medical equipment should call 555-0190 before March 23 to arrange support, which may include a temporary battery unit delivered to your home at no cost.\n\nIf crews finish ahead of schedule, power will be restored early. In the event of heavy rain, the work will move to the following Saturday, April 4, and a notice will be posted on our website by 6:00 P.M. on March 27. We appreciate your patience as we strengthen the local grid.\n\nTarrow Electric Cooperative\nCustomer Communications",
