    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Field Service Technicians\nFrom: Owen Gallagher, Metering Services Manager, Brightwater Utilities\nDate: April 7\nRe: Smart Meter Installation — Phase Two\n\nPhase two of our smart meter rollout begins May 5 and covers approximately 22,000 households in the Eastfield and Carver Heights districts. Phase one, completed in March, finished eleven days ahead of schedule thanks to your efficiency — thank you.\n\nFor phase two, please note the following adjustments. Installation appointments will now be offered in two-hour windows instead of four-hour windows, a change requested by customers in our post-phase-one survey. This means tighter routing; your daily schedules will be generated by the new dispatch software, and route changes must be cleared with dispatch rather than swapped informally between technicians.\n\nApartment buildings with banked meters require a property manager's signature before work begins. A list of buildings and manager contacts will be loaded onto your tablets. If a resident refuses an installation, do not attempt to persuade them; record the refusal in the system and move to the next appointment. The customer relations team will follow up separately.\n\nReplacement meters and lockable enclosures will be stocked at the Carver Depot rather than the central warehouse to cut travel time. Collect your first week's inventory there on May 2.",
