    "id": "p7-1118",
    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "Why was the reception desk moved?",
    "passage": "To: Vincent Okada <v.okada@okadahospitality.com>\nFrom: Renata Bilic <r.bilic@atelierhalcyon.com>\nSubject: Revised Lobby Design — Halcyon Bay Hotel\nDate: October 27\n\nDear Mr. Okada,\n\nThank you for your detailed comments on the schematic design we presented on October 20. Attached are revised drawings for the hotel lobby that respond to each of your three concerns.\n\nFirst, we have relocated the reception desk away from the main entrance to reduce congestion during group check-ins; it now sits beside the garden atrium, with a dedicated queuing area. Second, the skylight has been reduced from twelve meters to nine meters in length. Our engineers confirmed this change lowers the structural steel requirement enough to bring the lobby package back within your construction budget. Third, in place of imported marble flooring, we propose a locally quarried limestone that achieves a similar appearance at roughly sixty percent of the cost, with shorter delivery times.\n\nOne decision remains open: the mezzanine café. Extending the mezzanine would add seating for forty guests but would require resubmitting our permit application, adding an estimated six weeks to the approval process. We need your direction on this by November 7 to hold the current construction start date.\n\nCould your team join us for a review meeting during the first week of November? I am available any afternoon except Wednesday.\n\nKind regards,\nRenata Bilic, Principal Architect\nAtelier Halcyon",
