    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Staff, Calloway & Berg Accounting\nFrom: Diane Whitcomb, Managing Partner\nDate: January 9\nRe: Busy-Season Policies, February 1 - April 15\n\nAs we approach tax season, please review the firm's busy-season policies, which take effect February 1 and remain in place through April 15.\n\nScheduling. Core hours will be 9:00 A.M. to 7:00 P.M. on weekdays, and the office will be open on Saturdays from 9:00 A.M. to 2:00 P.M. Staff are expected to work one Saturday in three; the rotation schedule will be posted by January 23. Remote work remains available on Wednesdays only, as client document deliveries are lightest midweek.\n\nMeals and transportation. Staff working past 8:00 P.M. may order dinner through the firm's account, up to $25 per person, and may use a car service home at the firm's expense after 9:30 P.M. Receipts must be submitted within one week.\n\nTime off. Vacation requests during the busy season are suspended except in cases of emergency, which require approval from both your engagement manager and a partner. Vacation days already approved before January 9 will be honored.\n\nFinally, our annual post-season celebration is scheduled for April 24 at Harbor Hall. Families are welcome this year. Details will follow in March.",
