    "passage": "To: Gregory Tanaka <g.tanaka@bluefirgrill.com>\nFrom: Yusuf Demir <y.demir@pattersonbray.com>\nSubject: Outstanding Items for Your Year-End Financial Statements\nDate: February 3\n\nDear Mr. Tanaka,\n\nWe are making good progress on the year-end financial statements for Blue Fir Grill, and most of the records your bookkeeper provided in January were complete and well organized. However, three items are still outstanding, and we cannot finalize the statements without them.\n\n1. Bank statements for November and December for the payroll account. We received statements for the operating account only.\n2. Invoices supporting the kitchen equipment purchase recorded on October 12. The ledger shows a payment of $14,300, but no supplier invoice was attached, and we need it to classify the purchase correctly for depreciation.\n3. A signed copy of the amended lease for your patio expansion. The rent increase it contains affects the expense figures we report.\n\nPlease upload these to our client portal by February 14. Our engagement timeline assumed all records would be in hand by mid-February; if the documents arrive later, we may not complete the statements before your bank's March 2 deadline for your credit line renewal, and rush processing would involve additional fees.\n\nAs always, call me at extension 230 if anything is unclear.\n\nSincerely,\nYusuf Demir, CPA\nPatterson & Bray Accounting",
