    "id": "p7-1137",
    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What is one announced advantage of TrailLedger?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Employees, Renner Hodge Advisory\nFrom: Tomas Albrecht, Chief Financial Officer\nDate: September 14\nRe: New Expense Reporting System — TrailLedger\n\nOn October 1, the firm will retire its spreadsheet-based expense reporting process and adopt TrailLedger, a cloud-based system accessible from both desktop computers and mobile devices.\n\nThe key improvement is receipt capture: simply photograph a receipt with your phone, and TrailLedger extracts the vendor, date, and amount automatically. The system also flags any expense that falls outside firm policy — for example, hotel rates above the approved city limits — before the report reaches your supervisor, which should sharply reduce the back-and-forth corrections that currently delay reimbursements by up to two weeks.\n\nTo prepare for the transition, all employees must complete two steps by September 26: activate your TrailLedger account using the invitation e-mail sent on September 12, and verify the bank account on file for reimbursement deposits. Anyone who has not received an invitation should contact the finance help desk, since several invitations were returned due to outdated e-mail addresses in our records.\n\nImportant: expense reports begun in the old spreadsheet format must be submitted no later than September 30. The old system will become read-only on October 1, and incomplete drafts cannot be transferred to TrailLedger.\n\nBrief video tutorials are posted on the intranet under Finance Resources.",
    "options": [
      "It eliminates the need for supervisor approval.",
      "It automatically reads information from photographed receipts.",
      "It increases the firm's reimbursement limits.",
      "It pays employees in foreign currencies."
    ],
    "answer": 1,
