    "question": "What is the purpose of the visit described in the e-mail?",
    "passage": "To: All Staff, Helix Therapeutics\nFrom: Communications Office <comms@helixtherapeutics.com>\nSubject: Visit by Delegation from Osaka Research Partner — July 9\nDate: June 27\n\nDear Colleagues,\n\nOn Wednesday, July 9, Helix Therapeutics will host a six-member delegation from Kansai BioWorks, our development partner on the dermatology compound HX-117. The visit marks the start of the second phase of our joint research agreement, under which Kansai BioWorks will manufacture clinical supplies at its Osaka facility while our teams here lead the trial design.\n\nThe delegation will tour the formulation laboratories from 10:00 A.M. to 11:30 A.M. During this window, lab corridors on the second floor will be open to escorted visitors, so please ensure that confidential materials are cleared from whiteboards and benches by 9:30 A.M. Staff whose work involves projects unrelated to HX-117 should be prepared to pause demonstrations if asked, as our other pipeline programs are not covered by the partnership's confidentiality terms.\n\nA buffet lunch with the delegation will be held in the atrium at noon. All staff are welcome, and members of the HX-117 team are especially encouraged to attend. Please note that photography in the laboratories is prohibited for visitors and employees alike on that day; an approved photographer from the communications office will document the visit.\n\nQuestions may be sent to comms@helixtherapeutics.com by July 3.\n\nCommunications Office",
