    "type": "RC",
    "question": "Why was the memo written?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Staff, Grandview Power & Light\nFrom: Evelyn Marsh, Director of Human Resources\nDate: February 18\nRe: Storm Response Volunteer Roster — Spring Season\n\nEach spring, severe weather increases the likelihood of extended outages, and our storm response roster ensures we can restore service quickly. We are now seeking volunteers for the roster covering March 15 through June 15.\n\nField-qualified employees — line technicians, vegetation crews, and damage assessors — may sign up for on-call weeks, during which they must be reachable by phone and able to report within ninety minutes. On-call weeks carry a stipend of $300 in addition to overtime pay for any hours actually worked. Office staff can also contribute: during major events we need people to staff the customer information line, coordinate meal deliveries to crews, and log damage reports into the outage management system. Office volunteers receive overtime pay and a paid recovery day after any activation lasting more than twelve hours.\n\nNew this year, volunteers who complete a four-hour storm-role orientation by March 8 will be assigned to their preferred roles where possible. Orientation dates are February 26, March 3, and March 6, with both morning and evening options.\n\nLast spring's two major windstorms required 140 storm-role workers, and roster shortfalls meant some crews worked back-to-back shifts. A fuller roster this year will mean safer rotations for everyone. Sign up on the HR portal by March 1.",
