    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What is the main purpose of the e-mail?",
    "passage": "To: Department Managers, Crescent Harbor Bank\nFrom: Lionel Baptiste <l.baptiste@crescentharbor.com>\nSubject: Pilot Results and Expansion — Saturday Advisory Appointments\nDate: November 18\n\nDear Managers,\n\nI am writing to share the results of our three-month pilot offering financial advisory appointments on Saturday mornings at the Bayfront and Mill Creek branches, and to outline the next steps.\n\nThe pilot exceeded expectations. Across the two branches, advisors held 412 Saturday appointments, with seventy percent booked by customers who had never previously used our advisory services. Surveys show that most of these customers work weekday hours and had found our standard schedule impossible to use. Notably, appointment requests at Bayfront were nearly double those at Mill Creek, which we attribute to Bayfront's location beside a busy farmers market that operates on weekends.\n\nGiven these results, Saturday appointments will expand to six additional branches beginning January 10. Each participating branch will need two advisors and one service associate on a rotating Saturday schedule. Staff who volunteer for Saturday rotations will receive a weekday off in the same week plus a ten percent shift premium. Branch managers should submit staffing plans to me by December 5; where volunteers are insufficient, we will discuss alternatives before considering assigned rotations.\n\nPlease also review your branch's Saturday security procedures with your facilities coordinator before the launch, since several branches have not operated weekend hours in over a decade.\n\nRegards,\nLionel Baptiste\nSenior Vice President, Retail Banking",
