    "id": "p7-1177",
    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What prompted the updated guidelines?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Underwriting Staff, Cobalt Shield Insurance\nFrom: Henrik Olsen, Chief Underwriting Officer\nDate: April 21\nRe: Updated Guidelines for Coastal Property Policies\n\nFollowing our annual review of weather-related claims data, the company is updating its underwriting guidelines for residential properties located within three kilometers of the coastline. The new guidelines take effect for all policies quoted on or after May 12; quotes issued before that date remain valid under the old rules for their standard thirty-day period.\n\nTwo changes are central. First, properties in the affected zone will require a roof inspection report no more than five years old before a new policy can be issued. Homes with roofs over twenty years old will be referred to a senior underwriter rather than declined automatically, as replacement documentation or reinforcement work may justify standard terms. Second, the premium credit for storm shutters increases from five percent to eight percent, reflecting claims data showing that shuttered homes sustained markedly less window and water damage in last autumn's storms.\n\nPlease note that these guidelines apply to new business only. Renewal policies will follow a separate transition plan to be announced in June, and you should not apply the new requirements to renewals in the meantime.\n\nThe full guideline document, including revised rating tables, is available in the underwriting manual, section 12. A question-and-answer session will be held by videoconference on April 29 at 10:00 A.M.",
