    "id": "p7-1189",
    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "Why does the water authority flush hydrants?",
    "passage": "To: Residents of the Kingfisher Lane Service Area\nFrom: Clearstream Water Authority <updates@clearstreamwater.org>\nSubject: Hydrant Flushing Program — Week of October 6\nDate: September 25\n\nDear Customer,\n\nDuring the week of October 6, Clearstream Water Authority crews will conduct the autumn hydrant flushing program in your neighborhood. Flushing clears mineral sediment from water mains and verifies that hydrants will perform properly in an emergency. Work will take place between 9:00 A.M. and 3:00 P.M., Monday through Thursday, deliberately avoiding the morning hours when household water use is heaviest.\n\nWhat to expect: while crews are working nearby, you may notice reduced water pressure or temporary discoloration. Discolored water is caused by harmless mineral particles and is not a health risk; however, we recommend waiting until the water runs clear before doing laundry, as the particles can stain light-colored fabrics. If discoloration persists, run the cold tap closest to your water meter for several minutes.\n\nPlease also avoid parking within three meters of any hydrant during the work week. Vehicles blocking hydrant access are the most common cause of schedule delays, and crews are authorized to request towing where necessary.\n\nA street-by-street schedule is posted at clearstreamwater.org/flushing, and updates will be sent by text message to customers who have registered a mobile number on their account. There is no need to be home during the work, and no crew member will ever need to enter your residence for this program.\n\nClearstream Water Authority",
    "options": [
      "To lower customers' water bills",
      "To remove sediment from pipes and test hydrant readiness",
      "To install new water meters",
      "To detect illegal water connections"
    ],
    "answer": 1,
    "explanation": "첫 단락에서 소화전 방류는 상수도관의 광물 침전물을 제거하고 비상시 소화전이 제대로 작동하는지 확인하기 위한 작업이라고 설명하고 있습니다.",
