    "id": "p7-1193",
    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What is the purpose of the memo?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Project Architects and Designers, Castellan Rowe Architecture\nFrom: Beatrice Han, Director of Professional Development\nDate: September 3\nRe: Internal Mentorship Program — Applications Open\n\nApplications are now open for the third year of our internal mentorship program, which pairs early-career designers with senior architects for a nine-month cycle beginning November 1.\n\nThe program's value is well established. Of the fourteen designers mentored over the past two cycles, eleven have passed at least two sections of their professional licensing examinations, compared with a firm-wide average pass rate of fifty-four percent for non-participants. Mentored staff also reported higher satisfaction in last year's workplace survey, particularly regarding clarity of career paths.\n\nHow it works: pairs meet for at least two hours each month, and mentees may shadow their mentors at client presentations, consultant coordination meetings, and site walks. Each pair also completes one joint activity per quarter, such as a design competition entry or a conference presentation. Mentees receive twenty hours of billable-time relief per quarter to participate; mentors receive ten.\n\nEligibility: designers with two to six years of experience may apply as mentees. Architects with at least ten years of experience and a professional license may volunteer as mentors. We particularly encourage applications from our Riverside studio, which was underrepresented last cycle.\n\nApply through the professional development page by September 26. Pairings will be announced October 17 after a matching review that considers project types, career goals, and studio locations.",
