    "id": "p7-1197",
    "part": 7,
    "type": "RC",
    "question": "Why is the magazine changing its subscription model?",
    "passage": "To: Subscribers, Halverson Literary Quarterly\nFrom: Subscriptions Office <subscriptions@halversonquarterly.com>\nSubject: Important Changes to Your Subscription Options\nDate: January 28\n\nDear Subscriber,\n\nFor thirty-two years, Halverson Literary Quarterly has delivered new fiction, poetry, and criticism to readers in print. Beginning with our Summer issue, we are introducing changes to how the magazine is delivered and priced.\n\nRising paper and postage costs have made our current model difficult to sustain: printing and mailing now absorb sixty-one percent of each subscription dollar, leaving less for what matters most — paying our contributors. Rather than reduce writers' fees or page counts, we are restructuring our offerings.\n\nThree options will be available. The digital subscription, at $28 per year, includes each issue in three e-reader formats, complete access to our forty-year archive, and a monthly subscriber newsletter. The print-plus-digital subscription, at $52 per year, adds the quarterly print edition, now produced on heavier paper with improved binding. Finally, the patron tier, at $120 per year, includes everything above plus an invitation to our annual contributors' reading and your name in each issue's supporter list.\n\nCurrent print subscribers will be moved to print-plus-digital at their existing rate of $44 for one full renewal cycle — a savings of $8 — as thanks for your loyalty. After that cycle, standard pricing applies.\n\nTo select your option, log in at halversonquarterly.com/account before March 15. Subscribers who make no selection will continue receiving the print edition without interruption under the print-plus-digital plan.\n\nWith appreciation,\nThe Subscriptions Office",
    "options": [
      "Readership has declined sharply.",
      "Printing and mailing costs consume most subscription revenue.",
      "The magazine is merging with another publication.",
      "Contributors requested digital-only publication."
    ],
    "answer": 1,
    "explanation": "두 번째 단락에서 종이와 우편 요금 상승으로 인쇄·발송 비용이 구독료의 61%를 차지하여 기고자에게 지급할 몫이 줄어들기 때문에, 원고료나 지면을 줄이는 대신 구독 구조를 개편한다고 설명하고 있습니다.",
    "difficulty": "medium"
