    "type": "RC",
    "question": "Why is the office conducting the conservation trial?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All Staff, Hawthorne Gas & Electric, Riverbend Office\nFrom: Curtis Delgado, Facilities Manager\nDate: July 14\nRe: Building Energy Conservation Measures — August Trial\n\nAs an energy provider, we are often asked whether we follow the conservation advice we give customers. This August, the Riverbend office will pilot a set of internal conservation measures, and the results will be shared publicly in our autumn sustainability report.\n\nThe following changes will be in place from August 3 to August 31. Cooling setpoints will rise from 22 to 24 degrees Celsius in open work areas; conference rooms will remain at 22 degrees when booked. Lighting in corridors and storage areas will switch to occupancy sensors, which facilities crews will install during the last week of July, outside business hours. Window blinds on the south side of the building should be lowered by 11:00 A.M. each day — reminders will appear on the building's digital displays. Finally, the cafeteria will replace its two oldest refrigerated display cases, which together consume more electricity than all the office's printers combined.\n\nWe anticipate a reduction of roughly twelve percent in the building's August electricity use compared with last August. Staff who have concerns about workspace comfort — particularly those near the south windows — should contact the facilities help desk, and desk fans will be provided on request.\n\nIf the trial meets its target, the measures will be made permanent here and extended to our Lakeshore and Dunmore offices next year.",
