    "question": "What is the purpose of the article?",
    "passage": "Eastline Extension to Open Ahead of Schedule\n\nGRANVILLE (March 14) — The Granville Transit Authority (GTA) confirmed yesterday that the long-awaited Eastline light rail extension will open on May 3, nearly two months ahead of schedule. The 9-kilometer extension adds five stations and connects the Riverside business district with the university campus and the regional hospital. Trains will run every six minutes during peak hours and every twelve minutes at other times. GTA spokesperson Olivia Tran credited the early completion to mild winter weather and a decision to prefabricate track sections off-site, which reduced construction time by several months. The project, budgeted at $310 million, came in roughly $12 million under its original estimate. To mark the opening, the GTA will offer free rides on the entire Eastline during the first weekend of service. City officials predict the extension will remove up to 4,000 cars from downtown roads each weekday. Local business owners along the route, who endured two years of construction detours, say they are hopeful the new stations will bring back customers who had been avoiding the area.",
