    "question": "What is the purpose of the article?",
    "passage": "The Quiet Builder: A Profile of Renata Solis\n\nWhen Renata Solis founded GreenShell Packaging twelve years ago, she worked out of a rented garage with two employees and a single molding machine. Today, the company she leads produces compostable food containers for more than 2,000 restaurants and grocery chains, and it employs over 400 people at plants in Davenport and Kingsbury. Solis, who trained as a chemical engineer, spent her early career at a large plastics manufacturer, where she grew frustrated by the industry's slow response to environmental concerns. She left to develop a plant-fiber container that could break down in a home compost bin within eight weeks. The first two years were difficult; a modest loan from a regional development fund kept the company afloat while Solis refined her manufacturing process. Her persistence paid off when a national salad chain placed an order for five million containers. Despite GreenShell's growth, Solis still reviews product samples herself every Friday morning. \"The day I stop checking the details,\" she says, \"is the day we become ordinary.\" She is currently writing a book about sustainable manufacturing, due out next spring.",
