    "question": "What is the article mainly about?",
    "passage": "Grab and Go: Checkout-Free Stores Arrive in Welton\n\nShoppers at the new QuickShelf market on Danforth Avenue will notice something missing: cash registers. The store, which opened last week, uses ceiling-mounted cameras and weighted shelves to track which items each customer picks up. Shoppers scan a code on their phones when they enter, gather what they need, and simply walk out; a receipt arrives by e-mail minutes later. QuickShelf is the first checkout-free store in Welton, but it is unlikely to be the last. Its parent company, Arden Retail Group, plans to convert four more of its small-format stores to the technology by next summer. Company representatives say the system reduces waiting times and allows employees to spend more time restocking shelves and assisting customers. Not all shoppers are convinced. Some have expressed concern about how long the company keeps video data, while others simply prefer paying with cash, which the format does not accept. In response, Arden announced that one staffed counter will be added to each converted store for customers who want traditional service. The company says purchase records are deleted after ninety days and are never sold to outside firms.",
