    "passage": "Dunmore to Replace Entire Bus Fleet with Electric Models\n\nDUNMORE (Jan. 22) — The Dunmore City Council voted unanimously on Tuesday to replace all 140 of the city's diesel buses with battery-electric models over the next six years. [1] The first 25 electric buses will arrive in September and will operate on downtown routes, where officials say the reduction in exhaust and noise will be most noticeable. [2] The transition will cost an estimated $190 million, with about 40 percent covered by a federal clean-transit grant awarded last fall. [3] To support the new fleet, the city will build charging stations at both bus depots and install fast chargers at three major terminals. [4] Transit director Howard Nakamura acknowledged that electric buses cost roughly twice as much as diesel models up front but said they are cheaper to operate. \"Fuel and maintenance savings add up to about $40,000 per bus each year,\" he explained. \"Over a twelve-year service life, the economics clearly favor electric.\" The council also approved funds to retrain the city's 60 bus mechanics, who will complete a certification course in high-voltage systems at Dunmore Technical Institute.",
