    "passage": "FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\n\nHeliotek to Build Solar Panel Factory in Darrow County\n\nDARROW COUNTY (March 30) — Heliotek Industries announced today that it will construct a $620 million solar panel manufacturing plant on a 90-hectare site near the town of Lowfield, with production scheduled to begin in early 2028. The facility will produce next-generation thin-film panels and is expected to employ 1,100 workers at full capacity, making Heliotek the county's second-largest private employer. The company selected Darrow County after a two-year search that considered 14 locations in five states. County officials credited the area's existing rail connections, available workforce, and a recently approved property tax abatement for securing the project. As part of the agreement, Heliotek has committed to filling at least 70 percent of positions with county residents and will partner with Darrow Technical College to create a manufacturing certificate program beginning this autumn. Hiring for the first 200 positions, primarily in construction management and engineering, will begin in July. \"Demand for domestically produced panels has never been stronger,\" said Heliotek president Joanne Park. \"This plant lets us shorten delivery times for customers across the entire region.\" Site preparation is expected to begin within sixty days.",
