    "passage": "Carrowgate Airport Breaks Ground on Terminal C\n\nCARROWGATE (June 1) — With a ceremonial turn of a shovel on Friday, officials launched construction of Terminal C at Carrowgate Regional Airport, the facility's largest expansion since it opened in 1987. The $475 million terminal will add 16 gates, increasing the airport's capacity by roughly five million passengers per year. The project responds to a decade of steady growth: passenger numbers at Carrowgate have nearly doubled since 2016, and two international carriers began service there last year. Airport director Felicia Mwangi said the new terminal was designed with travelers' most common complaints in mind. Security screening lanes will be tripled, and the design places gates no more than an eight-minute walk from the checkpoint. The terminal will also feature a rooftop garden, locally owned restaurants rather than national chains, and a dedicated area for travelers with young children. During the three-year construction period, the airport will remain fully operational, though officials warn that the long-term parking lot nearest the site will close in August. A free shuttle will connect a newly opened overflow lot to all terminals every ten minutes. Terminal C is scheduled to welcome its first passengers in mid-2029.",
