    "question": "What does the Publishers Data Consortium report indicate?",
    "passage": "Listeners Drive Publishing's Fastest-Growing Format\n\nFor the eleventh consecutive year, audiobooks were the fastest-growing segment of the publishing industry, according to the annual report released Monday by the Publishers Data Consortium. [1] Audiobook revenue rose 14 percent last year, while print sales grew just 1 percent and e-book sales were flat. [2] The report links the growth to commuting and exercise habits; nearly half of surveyed listeners said they play audiobooks primarily while driving or working out. [3] The boom has changed how books are produced. Major publishers now record many titles in audio at the same time as the print edition, rather than months later, and some popular narrators have become selling points in their own right, with their names featured on covers. [4] The growth has also created opportunities for smaller players. Regional recording studios report full bookings, and several universities have added audiobook narration to their drama program curricula. Consortium analyst Devon Marsh cautioned that the format still represents only 11 percent of total industry revenue. \"Audio is the engine of growth,\" he said, \"but print remains the body of the business.\"",
