    "passage": "Streamline Secures Rights to Acclaimed Nature Series\n\nFRESHFORD (April 17) — Streaming service Veridia announced Tuesday that it has secured the exclusive global rights to Hidden Currents, the award-winning documentary series about deep-ocean ecosystems, beating several larger competitors in what industry observers describe as the most contested bidding war of the year. The four-part series, produced by independent studio Bluewater Films over six years, won the Meridian Prize for documentary filmmaking last autumn after its festival premiere. Under the agreement, reportedly worth $45 million, Veridia will release the series to subscribers in 60 countries this September and has ordered a second season, which Bluewater will begin filming in the Arctic next year. The deal continues Veridia's strategy of investing heavily in factual programming. The service, which has 38 million subscribers, devoted nearly a third of its content budget to documentaries last year—a far higher share than its rivals. Chief content officer Marcus Liang said internal data justifies the focus. \"Documentary viewers renew their subscriptions at higher rates than any other audience segment,\" he said. Bluewater founder Ines Castellanos said the partnership will fund equipment the small studio could never have afforded alone, including a deep-sea camera vehicle.",
