    "passage": "Verdant Grid Raises Funds to Expand Battery Network\n\nCOLEFAX (May 28) — Energy storage startup Verdant Grid announced Thursday that it has raised $75 million to expand its network of neighborhood battery stations, which store surplus solar power during the day and release it to the local grid in the evening. The three-year-old company currently operates 40 battery sites across the Colefax Valley, each roughly the size of a shipping container. The stations are installed on land leased from schools, churches, and shopping centers, which receive a share of the revenue the batteries earn. The new funding will allow Verdant Grid to build 120 additional sites over the next two years and to open a second operations center in Brindale. The model has proven popular with utilities, which pay the company for helping balance electricity supply during peak hours. Last summer, during a record heat wave, Verdant Grid's network supplied enough stored power each evening to serve 30,000 homes, helping the region avoid the rolling outages that affected neighboring counties. Founder and CEO Elias Toro, a former utility engineer, said the company will also begin testing larger stations near two retired power plants, where existing transmission lines can carry far more electricity.",
