    "question": "How often must the balances be calibrated?",
    "passage": "KESTREL LABORATORIES — QUALITY ASSURANCE NOTICE\n\nMONTHLY CALIBRATION OF ANALYTICAL BALANCES\n\nAll analytical balances in Rooms 210, 214, and 218 must be calibrated on the first working day of each month. Operators assigned to calibration duty should follow the steps below in order.\n\n1. Clean the weighing pan and the surrounding chamber with the supplied brush.\n2. Switch the balance on and allow it to warm up for at least 30 minutes before testing.\n3. Place the certified 100-gram reference weight (stored in the QA cabinet) at the center of the pan.\n4. Record the displayed reading in the calibration logbook kept beside each balance.\n5. The reading must fall within plus or minus 0.002 grams of 100 grams. If it does not, attach an OUT OF SERVICE tag to the balance and notify the quality assurance manager, Ms. Hana Sato, the same day.\n\nAfter a successful calibration, apply a dated green sticker to the front of the balance. Balances without a current sticker may not be used for client work under any circumstances.",
