    "type": "RC",
    "question": "How long are most items held?",
    "passage": "METRO TRANSIT AUTHORITY — LOST AND FOUND POLICY\n\nItems found on buses, trains, or station property are sent to the central Lost and Found office at 75 Terminal Plaza, Lower Level.\n\nHolding periods: Most items are held for 60 days from the date they are received. Wallets, identification cards, and passports are held for 30 days, after which identification documents are forwarded to the agencies that issued them. Perishable items, including food and beverages, are discarded within 24 hours for health reasons.\n\nClaiming an item: Owners must claim items in person on weekdays between 8:00 A.M. and 4:00 P.M. To claim an item, you must describe it in reasonable detail and present a photo ID. A claim inquiry may be started online at metrotransit.gov/lostfound, but items are never mailed or released to third parties without a signed authorization letter.\n\nUnclaimed items: At the end of the holding period, unclaimed items of value are sold at public auction, and the proceeds support the authority's reduced-fare program. Other items are donated to local charities.\n\nThe Metro Transit Authority is not responsible for items lost on its vehicles or property.",
