    "passage": "City of Dorset — Licensing Division\n12 Civic Square, Suite 110\n\nSeptember 2\n\nDear Mr. Felix Arnaud,\n\nOur records show that the operating license for Arnaud Catering (License No. 88231) will expire on September 30. To continue operating legally, you must renew the license before that date.\n\nHow to renew: The fastest method is online at dorsetcity.gov/licenses, where payment can be made by card or bank transfer. You may also renew by mail or in person at the Licensing Division. The standard renewal fee is $120. Your renewal must include a current certificate of liability insurance; renewals received without it cannot be processed.\n\nLate renewals: Licenses renewed between October 1 and October 31 are subject to a $30 late penalty in addition to the standard fee. Businesses still unlicensed after October 31 may not operate and are subject to a fine of $100 for each day of operation without a valid license.\n\nIf your business has closed or changed ownership, please notify this office in writing so that our records can be updated.\n\nSincerely,\nNadia Solomon\nLicensing Division Manager",
