    "type": "RC",
    "question": "What was the most popular reason for reading the magazine?",
    "passage": "Crestline Living Magazine — Reader Survey Results (Spring Issue)\nLast quarter, 2,150 subscribers completed our annual readership survey. Key findings:\n• 64% of respondents said they read the magazine primarily for home renovation features.\n• 58% wanted more short, practical articles of under two pages.\n• Only 19% reported reading the monthly celebrity interview, the lowest score of any regular section.\n• 47% said they would pay extra for a digital archive of past issues.\n• The gardening column received the highest satisfaction rating for the third consecutive year.\nRespondents aged 25-40 made up 51 percent of participants, a notable increase from 38 percent two years ago.\n\n--- Passage 2 ---\nMEMO\nTo: Editorial Staff\nFrom: Priya Raman, Editor in Chief\nDate: June 1\nRe: Content changes for the autumn issue\n\nHaving reviewed the survey results published in our spring issue, I am making the following changes beginning with the autumn issue. First, the celebrity interview will be discontinued; its page count will be reassigned to a new series of two-page renovation guides, which aligns with what most readers told us they want. Second, given the satisfaction ratings, Hannah Cho's column will be expanded from one page to two. Finally, the digital team will present a proposal for a paid online archive at the July planning meeting. Please send any concerns to me by June 12.\nPriya",
