    "passage": "To: Selected Pluma Users\nFrom: Pluma Software Team <beta@plumaapp.com>\nSubject: Invitation to the Pluma 4.0 Beta Program\nDate: February 10\n\nCongratulations! Because you have been an active Pluma note-taking app user for over two years, you are invited to test Pluma 4.0 before its public release in May. Beta highlights include an offline drawing mode, voice-to-text in six languages, and a redesigned search bar. Testers must use the app at least three hours per week and complete a feedback form every Friday during the eight-week program. In return, participants receive a free one-year Premium subscription when version 4.0 launches. Spaces are limited to 500 testers. To join, sign the testing agreement at plumaapp.com/beta by February 17.\n\n--- Passage 2 ---\nPluma 4.0 Beta — Week 3 Feedback Form\nTester: Marcus Aldridge\nDate: March 6\nHours used this week: 5\n\nOverall impressions: The redesigned search bar is excellent—results appear noticeably faster than in version 3.5. The offline drawing mode, however, has a recurring problem: sketches created without an Internet connection disappear if the app closes before syncing. I lost a full page of meeting notes this way on Tuesday. Voice-to-text worked well in English and Spanish, though I have not tested other languages. One suggestion: add an automatic local backup for offline sketches. Despite the bug, I am enjoying the program and look forward to claiming the subscription reward at launch.",
