    "passage": "MERIDIAN HOTELS — CHANGES TO THE HORIZONS REWARDS PROGRAM\nEffective July 1\nWe are updating Horizons Rewards to make earning simpler:\n• Members will earn 10 points per dollar spent on room rates, up from 8.\n• Points will now also be earned on dining charges billed to your room.\n• Points will expire after 24 months of account inactivity, instead of the previous 18 months.\n• Free-night redemptions will start at 25,000 points for standard rooms.\n• As a transition benefit, any stay completed between July 1 and August 31 earns double points.\nPoints earned before July 1 keep their current value. Questions? Contact rewards@meridianhotels.com.\n\n--- Passage 2 ---\nTo: rewards@meridianhotels.com\nFrom: Beatriz Solano <b.solano@quickpost.net>\nSubject: Missing points from my August stay\nDate: September 4\n\nHello,\nI stayed at the Meridian Lakeshore from August 12 to 15 and paid $200 per night for three nights. Under the transition benefit announced for this summer, I expected my room charges to earn 12,000 points, but my statement shows only 6,000. It appears the double-points promotion was not applied. Could you correct this? Also, my statement does not include any points for the $90 dinner I billed to my room on August 13. Since the updated rules say dining charges now earn points, I believe those are missing as well. My membership number is HR-558214. Thank you for checking.\nBeatriz Solano",
