    "passage": "FOR LEASE — Merchant's Row Tower, Suite 410\n2,800 square feet of open-plan office space on the fourth floor. Rent: $4,200 per month; minimum lease term of three years. Two reserved parking spaces included. Tenants pay their own utilities. Available September 1. Large windows, recently updated elevators, and a five-minute walk to Central Station. To arrange a tour, contact Dana Whitfield, Pinnacle Realty, at d.whitfield@pinnaclerealty.com.\n\n--- Passage 2 ---\nMEMO\nTo: Renata Kowalski, CEO\nFrom: Tom Garza, Operations Manager\nDate: July 8\nRe: Tour of Merchant's Row Tower, Suite 410\n\nI toured the suite this morning. The space is bright, the layout suits our team of twenty, and the location near transit is ideal. However, the carpet is badly worn throughout, and only two parking spaces are included even though we need four for our sales staff. I recommend we offer $3,900 per month and ask the landlord to replace the carpet before we move in.\n\n--- Passage 3 ---\nTo: t.garza@kowalskiconsulting.com\nFrom: d.whitfield@pinnaclerealty.com\nDate: July 15\nSubject: Suite 410 — Owner's response\n\nDear Mr. Garza,\nThank you for your interest in Suite 410. I have discussed your terms with the building's owner. He is willing to replace the carpet in the entire suite before your move-in date. He can also offer two additional reserved parking spaces at $75 each per month. The monthly rent, however, must remain at $4,200; instead, he will waive the first month's rent entirely on a three-year lease. Please let me know by July 22 whether you would like to proceed with a lease agreement.\nBest regards,\nDana Whitfield",
