    "passage": "GREENFIELD CHAMBER OF COMMERCE\nSmall Business Excellence Award — Nomination Guidelines\nEligibility: Nominees must have operated within Greenfield for at least three years and employ fewer than 50 people. Any resident may nominate a business by submitting a letter describing the business's contributions to the community. Nomination letters are due by March 31. The winner will be announced at the Chamber's gala on May 6 and will receive a $5,000 grant along with a feature article in Commerce Quarterly magazine.\n\n--- Passage 2 ---\nMarch 24\nDear Selection Committee,\nI am writing to nominate Birch & Vine Café for the Small Business Excellence Award. The café has been a fixture on Walnut Street for six years and employs eighteen local residents. Beyond serving excellent food, the café hosts monthly fund-raisers for the Greenfield Food Pantry and runs a composting program with the community garden. Owner Sam Whitaker also offers free barista training to high school students each summer. Few businesses give back to our town so generously.\nSincerely,\nOlivia Tran\n\n--- Passage 3 ---\nPRESS RELEASE — May 7\nThe Greenfield Chamber of Commerce is pleased to announce that Birch & Vine Café has won this year's Small Business Excellence Award. Owner Sam Whitaker accepted the award at last night's gala before an audience of nearly 300 guests. The judging panel cited the café's deep community involvement, particularly its support of local charitable causes. Mr. Whitaker said the grant will be used to expand the café's summer job-training program for students. A profile of the café will appear in the summer issue of Commerce Quarterly.",
