    "passage": "NOTICE — ASHFORD PUBLIC LIBRARY\nThe library will close on July 1 for a major renovation and will remain closed through August 30. During the closure, our bookmobile will visit five neighborhood locations each week; the schedule is posted at ashfordlibrary.org. The outdoor book drop will remain open, and due dates for all borrowed items have been extended to September 8. Please join us for a reopening celebration on Saturday, September 6, featuring author talks and children's activities.\n\n--- Passage 2 ---\nashfordlibrary.org/volunteer\nVOLUNTEERS NEEDED — Help Us Move!\nBefore renovation begins, we need volunteers to help pack and move parts of our collection to temporary storage. Work dates: June 23–28, with morning shifts (9:00 A.M.–noon) and afternoon shifts (1:00–4:00 P.M.). Volunteers will receive a commemorative T-shirt and an invitation to a special preview night on September 5, the evening before the library reopens to the public. Sign up using the form below by June 15. No lifting experience necessary; carts will be provided.\n\n--- Passage 3 ---\nTo: k.osei@plummail.net\nFrom: m.delgado@ashfordlibrary.org\nDate: June 17\nSubject: Thank you for volunteering!\n\nDear Mr. Osei,\nThank you for signing up for three afternoon shifts during our moving week. Please wear closed-toe shoes and use the parking lot behind the building, as the front lot will be occupied by moving trucks. As a volunteer, you will receive your invitation to the preview night by mail in August. One more thing: we will also need help reshelving books during the last week of August, before the public reopening. If you are available then, simply reply to this e-mail and I will add you to the list.\nWarm regards,\nMaria Delgado, Head Librarian",
