    "passage": "RIVERSIDE FARMERS MARKET — VENDOR GUIDELINES\nThe market operates every Saturday, 8:00 A.M.–1:00 P.M., from May through October. Vendors must grow or make all products themselves within 100 miles of Riverside. Booth fees: $35 per week or $400 for the full season. All vendors must submit a current certificate of liability insurance with their application. Applications are reviewed at the end of each month, and decisions are sent within two weeks. Questions? Contact market manager Doug Reyes at vendors@riversidemarket.org.\n\n--- Passage 2 ---\nVENDOR APPLICATION — Riverside Farmers Market\nBusiness name: Maple Hollow Apiary | Applicant: Hannah Cho\nProducts: Raw honey, honeycomb, beeswax candles (all produced at our apiary)\nDistance from Riverside: 40 miles\nBooth preference: Full season\nLocation request: A corner booth near the main entrance, if possible\nInsurance: Certificate of liability insurance attached\nDate submitted: March 28\n\n--- Passage 3 ---\nTo: h.cho@maplehollow.com\nFrom: vendors@riversidemarket.org\nDate: April 9\nSubject: Application approved!\n\nDear Ms. Cho,\nWelcome to the Riverside Farmers Market! Your application has been approved, and your season fee is due by April 15. Regarding your location request: corner booths are assigned by seniority, so as a first-year vendor you have been placed on the waiting list for one, and you will start at booth 22 in the central aisle. All new vendors must attend an orientation on Saturday, April 26, at 10:00 A.M. at the market office. The first market day of the season is May 2. We look forward to having Maple Hollow Apiary with us!\nBest,\nDoug Reyes, Market Manager",
